('q_bio_2023_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Antibodies are produced by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Red blood cells", "B. Platelets", "C. White blood cells", "D. Plasma"]', 'C', 'White blood cells (specifically B lymphocytes) produce antibodies as part of the immune response.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The condition where the eye cannot focus on near objects is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Myopia", "B. Hypermetropia", "C. Astigmatism", "D. Presbyopia"]', 'B', 'Hypermetropia (farsightedness) is a condition where close objects appear blurry because the image focuses behind the retina.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Urea is produced in the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Kidney", "B. Liver", "C. Lungs", "D. Skin"]', 'B', 'Urea is produced in the liver through the deamination of amino acids and is then excreted by the kidneys.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The reflex arc consists of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Receptor, sensory neuron, brain, motor neuron, effector", "B. Receptor, sensory neuron, relay neuron, motor neuron, effector", "C. Brain, spinal cord, muscles", "D. Eyes, brain, hands"]', 'B', 'A reflex arc includes receptor, sensory neuron, relay neuron (in spinal cord), motor neuron, and effector.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Photosynthesis occurs mainly in the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Root", "B. Stem", "C. Leaf", "D. Flower"]', 'C', 'Photosynthesis mainly occurs in leaves because they contain chloroplasts and have a large surface area for light absorption.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The tissue responsible for water transport in plants is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Phloem", "B. Xylem", "C. Cambium", "D. Epidermis"]', 'B', 'Xylem tissue transports water and dissolved minerals from roots to leaves through transpiration pull.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Stomata are mainly found on the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Upper surface of leaves", "B. Lower surface of leaves", "C. Roots", "D. Flowers"]', 'B', 'Stomata are mainly found on the lower epidermis of leaves to reduce water loss while allowing gas exchange.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The hormone that promotes cell elongation in plants is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ethylene", "B. Auxin", "C. Abscisic acid", "D. Cytokinin"]', 'B', 'Auxin promotes cell elongation, especially in shoots, and is involved in phototropism and gravitropism.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Pollination is the transfer of pollen from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Stigma to ovary", "B. Anther to stigma", "C. Ovary to ovule", "D. Style to stigma"]', 'B', 'Pollination is the transfer of pollen grains from the anther (male part) to the stigma (female part) of a flower.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Natural selection was proposed by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gregor Mendel", "B. Charles Darwin", "C. Jean Lamarck", "D. Louis Pasteur"]', 'B', 'Charles Darwin proposed the theory of evolution by natural selection in his book "On the Origin of Species."', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Homologous structures indicate:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Convergent evolution", "B. Common ancestry", "C. No relationship", "D. Parallel evolution"]', 'B', 'Homologous structures have similar anatomy but different functions, indicating common evolutionary ancestry.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The term "survival of the fittest" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only the strongest survive", "B. The best adapted organisms survive to reproduce", "C. Fighting for survival", "D. Living the longest"]', 'B', 'Survival of the fittest means organisms best adapted to their environment are more likely to survive and reproduce.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Transpiration is important because it:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Produces food", "B. Creates transpiration pull for water movement", "C. Produces oxygen", "D. Fixes nitrogen"]', 'B', 'Transpiration creates a pulling force (transpiration pull) that draws water up through the xylem from roots to leaves.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2023_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Fossils provide evidence for evolution because they:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Are found in all rocks", "B. Show changes in organisms over time", "C. Are always complete", "D. Are found in water only"]', 'B', 'Fossils show how organisms have changed over geological time, providing evidence for evolutionary transitions.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The cell membrane is primarily made up of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Proteins only", "B. Lipids only", "C. Phospholipid bilayer and proteins", "D. Carbohydrates only"]', 'C', 'The cell membrane consists of a phospholipid bilayer with embedded proteins.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Which organelle is responsible for aerobic respiration?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Nucleus", "B. Ribosome", "C. Mitochondrion", "D. Golgi apparatus"]', 'C', 'Mitochondria are the sites of aerobic respiration, producing ATP.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The rough endoplasmic reticulum has ribosomes attached to it and is involved in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Lipid synthesis", "B. Protein synthesis", "C. Carbohydrate storage", "D. Cell division"]', 'B', 'Rough ER with ribosomes synthesizes proteins for secretion.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'During mitosis, chromosomes are visible in which phase?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Interphase", "B. Prophase", "C. Metaphase", "D. Cytokinesis"]', 'B', 'Chromosomes condense and become visible in prophase.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The cell wall is present in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Animal cells only", "B. Plant cells only", "C. Both plant and animal cells", "D. Neither plant nor animal cells"]', 'B', 'Plant cells have cell walls made of cellulose; animal cells do not.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The process by which cells obtain energy without oxygen is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Aerobic respiration", "B. Photosynthesis", "C. Anaerobic respiration", "D. Transpiration"]', 'C', 'Anaerobic respiration releases energy without using oxygen.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Active transport differs from diffusion because it:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Does not require energy", "B. Moves substances down a concentration gradient", "C. Requires energy to move substances against concentration gradient", "D. Only occurs in plants"]', 'C', 'Active transport uses ATP to move substances against their gradient.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The stage of mitosis where chromosomes align at the cell''s equator is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Prophase", "B. Metaphase", "C. Anaphase", "D. Telophase"]', 'B', 'In metaphase, chromosomes line up at the metaphase plate/equator.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Chloroplasts are found in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. All cells", "B. Only animal cells", "C. Only plant cells and algae", "D. Only bacteria"]', 'C', 'Chloroplasts are the sites of photosynthesis in plants and algae.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Meiosis produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Two identical cells", "B. Four identical cells", "C. Four genetically different cells", "D. One large cell"]', 'C', 'Meiosis produces four genetically different haploid cells.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The basic unit of heredity is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Chromosome", "B. Cell", "C. Gene", "D. Nucleotide"]', 'C', 'Genes are segments of DNA that code for specific traits.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'If both parents are heterozygous (Aa), the probability of having an offspring with genotype aa is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 25%", "B. 50%", "C. 75%", "D. 100%"]', 'A', 'Aa × Aa gives AA:Aa:Aa:aa = 1:2:1, so 25% are aa.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The complementary base pair to Adenine in DNA is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Guanine", "B. Cytosine", "C. Thymine", "D. Uracil"]', 'C', 'In DNA, Adenine pairs with Thymine (A-T).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Sex-linked traits are usually carried on the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Y chromosome only", "B. X chromosome", "C. Autosomes", "D. Mitochondrial DNA"]', 'B', 'Most sex-linked traits are on the X chromosome.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'A mutation is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Normal cell division", "B. A change in DNA sequence", "C. Protein synthesis", "D. Cell death"]', 'B', 'Mutations are changes in the nucleotide sequence of DNA.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Sickle cell disease is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Viral infection", "B. Bacterial infection", "C. Gene mutation", "D. Nutritional deficiency"]', 'C', 'Sickle cell disease results from a mutation in the hemoglobin gene.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The genotype of a carrier of a recessive trait is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Homozygous dominant", "B. Homozygous recessive", "C. Heterozygous", "D. None of the above"]', 'C', 'Carriers are heterozygous - they carry one recessive allele but don''t express it.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_bio_2024_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The Human Genome Project aimed to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Clone humans", "B. Map all human genes", "C. Create new species", "D. Cure all diseases"]', 'B', 'The Human Genome Project mapped the entire human genetic sequence.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Blood type in humans is an example of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Simple dominance", "B. Incomplete dominance", "C. Codominance", "D. Sex linkage"]', 'C', 'ABO blood types show codominance (A and B) and multiple alleles.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Down syndrome is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gene mutation", "B. Extra copy of chromosome 21", "C. Missing X chromosome", "D. Extra Y chromosome"]', 'B', 'Down syndrome (Trisomy 21) results from three copies of chromosome 21.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'A food chain always starts with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Consumers", "B. Decomposers", "C. Producers", "D. Predators"]', 'C', 'Producers (autotrophs) form the base of food chains.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'An ecosystem consists of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only living organisms", "B. Only non-living factors", "C. Both living organisms and their physical environment", "D. Only plants"]', 'C', 'An ecosystem includes biotic (living) and abiotic (non-living) components.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The nitrogen cycle involves:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only plants", "B. Only bacteria", "C. Plants, animals, bacteria, and the atmosphere", "D. Only animals"]', 'C', 'The nitrogen cycle involves various organisms and the atmosphere.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Organisms that break down dead organic matter are called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Producers", "B. Consumers", "C. Decomposers", "D. Parasites"]', 'C', 'Decomposers (bacteria and fungi) break down dead organic matter.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Symbiosis where both organisms benefit is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Parasitism", "B. Commensalism", "C. Mutualism", "D. Predation"]', 'C', 'Mutualism is a symbiotic relationship benefiting both organisms.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'Eutrophication is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Lack of nutrients", "B. Excess nutrients in water bodies", "C. High oxygen levels", "D. Cold temperatures"]', 'B', 'Eutrophication results from excess nutrients causing algal blooms.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'The greenhouse effect is primarily caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Oxygen", "B. Nitrogen", "C. Carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases", "D. Hydrogen"]', 'C', 'CO₂ and other greenhouse gases trap heat in the atmosphere.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_bio_2024_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_bio_2024_1', 'A population is defined as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. All organisms in an area", "B. Organisms of the same species in an area", "C. All plants in an area", "D. All animals in an area"]', 'B', 'A population consists of organisms of the same species in a defined area.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
