('q_ca_meth_002', 'topic_ca_costing', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Job costing is suitable for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Mass production","Custom or unique orders","Continuous production","Identical products"]', 'B', 'Job costing is used when products are made to customer specifications or are unique.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_meth_003', 'topic_ca_costing', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Process costing is used when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Each product is unique","Products pass through continuous processes","Only one product is made","There is no production"]', 'Products pass through continuous processes', 'Process costing is used for continuous production where products are identical and pass through defined processes.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_meth_004', 'topic_ca_costing', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Marginal costing treats fixed costs as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Product costs","Period costs","Variable costs","Direct costs"]', 'Period costs', 'In marginal costing, fixed costs are treated as period costs charged entirely against the period''s revenue.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_meth_005', 'topic_ca_costing', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Contribution margin equals:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Sales - Fixed costs","Sales - Variable costs","Fixed costs - Variable costs","Total costs - Sales"]', 'Sales - Variable costs', 'Contribution = Sales Revenue - Variable Costs. It contributes towards covering fixed costs and profit.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_oh_002', 'topic_ca_overhead', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Apportionment of overheads is done when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Costs can be directly traced","Costs are shared between cost centers","There is only one department","Costs are ignored"]', 'B', 'Apportionment distributes common costs between departments based on appropriate bases.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_oh_003', 'topic_ca_overhead', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Absorption rate is calculated as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total overhead ÷ Activity level","Revenue ÷ Cost","Profit × 100","Materials + Labor"]', 'Total overhead ÷ Activity level', 'Overhead Absorption Rate = Budgeted Overhead / Budgeted Activity Level (labor hours, machine hours, etc.).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_oh_004', 'topic_ca_overhead', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Under-absorption of overhead occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Actual overhead is less than absorbed","Actual overhead exceeds absorbed overhead","Overheads equal absorption","There are no overheads"]', 'B', 'Under-absorption occurs when actual overheads are greater than the amount absorbed/recovered.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_ca_oh_005', 'topic_ca_overhead', 'subj_wassce_cost_accounting', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Machine hour rate is appropriate when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Production is labor-intensive","Production is machine-intensive","There are no machines","Only in service industries"]', 'Production is machine-intensive', 'Machine hour rate is used when production is predominantly machine-based.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_001', 'topic_atomic', 'subj_nsmq_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'How many protons, neutrons, and electrons are in ²³Na (sodium-23)?', 'direct_answer', 'round_one', NULL, '11 protons, 12 neutrons, 11 electrons', 'Na has atomic number 11, so 11 protons and electrons. Neutrons = 23 - 11 = 12', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_002', 'topic_stoichiometry', 'subj_nsmq_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What is the molar mass of H₂SO₄?', 'direct_answer', 'round_one', NULL, '98 g/mol', 'H₂SO₄: 2(1) + 32 + 4(16) = 2 + 32 + 64 = 98 g/mol', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_003', 'topic_bonding', 'subj_nsmq_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What type of bond forms between sodium and chlorine?', 'direct_answer', 'round_one', NULL, 'Ionic bond', 'Sodium (metal) transfers an electron to chlorine (non-metal), forming Na⁺ and Cl⁻ ions', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_004', 'topic_equilibrium', 'subj_nsmq_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For the reaction N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃, write the expression for Kc', 'direct_answer', 'round_one', NULL, 'Kc = [NH₃]²/([N₂][H₂]³)', 'Products over reactants, each raised to their stoichiometric coefficient', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_005', 'topic_organic', 'subj_nsmq_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What is the IUPAC name of CH₃CH₂CH₂OH?', 'direct_answer', 'round_one', NULL, 'Propan-1-ol or 1-propanol', '3-carbon alcohol with OH on carbon 1', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The atomic number of an element is determined by the number of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Neutrons", "B. Protons", "C. Electrons", "D. Nucleons"]', 'B', 'The atomic number equals the number of protons in the nucleus, which determines the element identity.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Isotopes of an element have the same number of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Neutrons", "B. Mass number", "C. Protons", "D. Nucleons"]', 'C', 'Isotopes have the same number of protons (same atomic number) but different numbers of neutrons.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The electron configuration of sodium (Na, Z=11) is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 2,8,2", "B. 2,8,1", "C. 2,9", "D. 2,8,8"]', 'B', 'Sodium has 11 electrons arranged as 2,8,1 in the first three energy levels.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Which subatomic particle has no charge?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Proton", "B. Electron", "C. Neutron", "D. Ion"]', 'C', 'Neutrons are electrically neutral particles found in the nucleus along with protons.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The mass number is the sum of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Protons and electrons", "B. Protons and neutrons", "C. Neutrons and electrons", "D. Protons only"]', 'B', 'Mass number = number of protons + number of neutrons (nucleons in the nucleus).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'An atom with 17 protons and 18 neutrons has a mass number of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 17", "B. 18", "C. 35", "D. 1"]', 'C', 'Mass number = protons + neutrons = 17 + 18 = 35.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The maximum number of electrons in the second energy level is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 2", "B. 8", "C. 18", "D. 32"]', 'B', 'The maximum electrons in each shell follows 2n², so the second shell (n=2) holds maximum 8 electrons.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Which scientist proposed the nuclear model of the atom?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Dalton", "B. Thomson", "C. Rutherford", "D. Bohr"]', 'C', 'Ernest Rutherford proposed the nuclear model based on his gold foil experiment, showing a dense positive nucleus.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Cations are formed when atoms:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gain electrons", "B. Lose electrons", "C. Share electrons", "D. Gain protons"]', 'B', 'Cations (positive ions) are formed when atoms lose electrons, resulting in more protons than electrons.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The relative atomic mass of chlorine is 35.5 because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. It has 35.5 protons", "B. It is a mixture of isotopes", "C. It has 35.5 neutrons", "D. It is radioactive"]', 'B', 'Chlorine exists as two isotopes (Cl-35 and Cl-37) in nature, giving an average relative atomic mass of 35.5.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'An ionic bond is formed between:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Two metals", "B. Two non-metals", "C. A metal and a non-metal", "D. Two noble gases"]', 'C', 'Ionic bonds form when a metal transfers electrons to a non-metal, creating oppositely charged ions that attract.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The bond in hydrogen chloride (HCl) is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ionic", "B. Covalent", "C. Metallic", "D. Hydrogen bond"]', 'B', 'HCl has a covalent bond where hydrogen and chlorine share electrons.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Which compound has a giant covalent structure?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sodium chloride", "B. Water", "C. Diamond", "D. Methane"]', 'C', 'Diamond has a giant covalent structure where each carbon atom is covalently bonded to four other carbon atoms.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Metallic bonding involves:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Transfer of electrons", "B. Sharing of electron pairs", "C. Delocalized electrons", "D. Hydrogen bonds"]', 'C', 'Metallic bonding involves a sea of delocalized electrons shared among positive metal ions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The shape of a water molecule is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Linear", "B. Trigonal planar", "C. Bent/Angular", "D. Tetrahedral"]', 'C', 'Water has a bent shape due to two lone pairs on oxygen pushing the hydrogen atoms closer together.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Van der Waals forces are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Strong intermolecular forces", "B. Weak intermolecular forces", "C. Intramolecular forces", "D. Ionic forces"]', 'B', 'Van der Waals forces are weak intermolecular attractions between molecules, including London dispersion forces.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'A coordinate covalent bond is one where:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Both atoms donate electrons", "B. One atom donates both electrons", "C. Electrons are transferred", "D. No electrons are shared"]', 'B', 'In a coordinate (dative) covalent bond, one atom provides both electrons to the shared pair.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Graphite conducts electricity because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. It contains ions", "B. It has metallic bonds", "C. It has delocalized electrons", "D. It contains water"]', 'C', 'Graphite has delocalized electrons between its carbon layers that are free to move and conduct electricity.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Hydrogen bonding is strongest in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. HCl", "B. H2O", "C. H2S", "D. CH4"]', 'B', 'Water has strong hydrogen bonding because oxygen is highly electronegative and small, creating strong H-bonds.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The bond angle in methane (CH4) is approximately:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 90°", "B. 104.5°", "C. 109.5°", "D. 120°"]', 'C', 'Methane has a tetrahedral shape with bond angles of approximately 109.5°.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The pH of a neutral solution is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 0", "B. 7", "C. 14", "D. 1"]', 'B', 'A neutral solution has a pH of 7, where the concentration of H+ equals OH- ions.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Which indicator turns pink in alkaline solution?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Methyl orange", "B. Litmus", "C. Phenolphthalein", "D. Bromothymol blue"]', 'C', 'Phenolphthalein is colorless in acid and turns pink in alkaline solutions.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'When an acid reacts with a base, the products are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Salt only", "B. Water only", "C. Salt and water", "D. Salt and hydrogen"]', 'C', 'Neutralization: Acid + Base → Salt + Water. This is a neutralization reaction.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'A strong acid is one that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Has a high pH", "B. Is completely ionized in solution", "C. Is partially ionized", "D. Does not conduct electricity"]', 'B', 'Strong acids completely dissociate in water, releasing all their hydrogen ions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The salt formed when HCl reacts with NaOH is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sodium sulfate", "B. Sodium chloride", "C. Sodium nitrate", "D. Sodium carbonate"]', 'B', 'HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H2O. Sodium chloride (table salt) is formed.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Effervescence occurs when acids react with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Oxides", "B. Hydroxides", "C. Carbonates", "D. Sulfates"]', 'C', 'Carbonates react with acids to produce carbon dioxide gas, causing effervescence (bubbling).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'A buffer solution:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Changes pH rapidly", "B. Resists changes in pH", "C. Has pH of 14", "D. Contains only acids"]', 'B', 'A buffer solution resists changes in pH when small amounts of acid or base are added.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'Hydrochloric acid is a:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Weak acid", "B. Strong acid", "C. Weak base", "D. Strong base"]', 'B', 'Hydrochloric acid (HCl) is a strong acid that completely dissociates in water.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2023_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2023_1', 'The basicity of H2SO4 is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1", "B. 2", "C. 3", "D. 4"]', 'B', 'Sulfuric acid (H2SO4) has basicity of 2 as it can donate two hydrogen ions per molecule.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
