('q_chem_2024_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The pH of a 0.01M HCl solution is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1", "B. 2", "C. 12", "D. 13"]', 'B', 'pH = -log[H⁺] = -log(0.01) = 2.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'A buffer solution:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Has pH of exactly 7", "B. Resists changes in pH when small amounts of acid or base are added", "C. Contains only a strong acid", "D. Always has a high pH"]', 'B', 'Buffers maintain relatively constant pH upon addition of small amounts of acid or base.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Neutralization produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Salt and hydrogen", "B. Salt and water", "C. Salt and oxygen", "D. Salt and carbon dioxide"]', 'B', 'Acid + Base → Salt + Water (neutralization).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Which is a strong acid?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Acetic acid", "B. Carbonic acid", "C. Hydrochloric acid", "D. Citric acid"]', 'C', 'HCl is a strong acid that completely dissociates in water.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'An indicator that is red in acid and blue in base is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Phenolphthalein", "B. Litmus", "C. Methyl orange", "D. Bromothymol blue"]', 'B', 'Litmus is red in acid and blue in base/alkali.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Efflorescence is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Absorption of water from air", "B. Loss of water of crystallization to the atmosphere", "C. Dissolution in water", "D. Formation of crystals"]', 'B', 'Efflorescent substances lose water of crystallization to the air.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Deliquescence is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Loss of water to atmosphere", "B. Absorption of water from air to form a solution", "C. Evaporation", "D. Crystallization"]', 'B', 'Deliquescent substances absorb moisture and eventually dissolve.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Oxidation is defined as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Loss of electrons", "B. Gain of electrons", "C. Loss of protons", "D. Gain of protons"]', 'A', 'Oxidation is loss of electrons (OIL RIG - Oxidation Is Loss).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'In electrolysis, reduction occurs at the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Anode", "B. Cathode", "C. Both electrodes", "D. Electrolyte"]', 'B', 'Cations move to cathode where they gain electrons (reduction).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The oxidation state of sulfur in H₂SO₄ is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. +4", "B. +6", "C. -2", "D. +2"]', 'B', 'In H₂SO₄: 2(+1) + S + 4(-2) = 0, so S = +6.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'A reducing agent is a substance that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gains electrons", "B. Loses electrons", "C. Gains protons", "D. Loses protons"]', 'B', 'A reducing agent loses electrons (gets oxidized) to reduce something else.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'During the electrolysis of brine, chlorine gas is produced at the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Cathode", "B. Anode", "C. Both electrodes", "D. Neither electrode"]', 'B', 'Chloride ions are oxidized at the anode: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Electroplating is used for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Extracting metals", "B. Coating metals with other metals", "C. Producing electricity", "D. Breaking down compounds"]', 'B', 'Electroplating deposits a thin layer of metal on an object.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'A galvanic cell converts:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Electrical energy to chemical energy", "B. Chemical energy to electrical energy", "C. Heat energy to electrical energy", "D. Light energy to electrical energy"]', 'B', 'Galvanic/voltaic cells convert chemical energy to electrical energy.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The functional group of alcohols is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. -CHO", "B. -OH", "C. -COOH", "D. -CO-"]', 'B', 'Alcohols contain the hydroxyl (-OH) functional group.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Alkenes contain:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only single bonds", "B. At least one double bond", "C. At least one triple bond", "D. No carbon-hydrogen bonds"]', 'B', 'Alkenes have at least one C=C double bond.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
