('q_chem_2024_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The general formula for alkanes is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. CₙH₂ₙ", "B. CₙH₂ₙ₊₂", "C. CₙH₂ₙ₋₂", "D. CₙHₙ"]', 'B', 'Alkanes have the general formula CₙH₂ₙ₊₂ (saturated hydrocarbons).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Isomers are compounds that have:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Same molecular formula but different structures", "B. Same structure but different formula", "C. Different atoms", "D. Same properties"]', 'A', 'Isomers have the same molecular formula but different structural arrangements.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Fermentation of glucose produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ethanol and oxygen", "B. Ethanol and carbon dioxide", "C. Methanol and water", "D. Ethanoic acid and water"]', 'B', 'C₆H₁₂O₆ → 2C₂H₅OH + 2CO₂ (fermentation).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The IUPAC name of CH₃CH₂OH is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Methanol", "B. Ethanol", "C. Propanol", "D. Ethene"]', 'B', 'CH₃CH₂OH is ethanol (2 carbons with -OH group).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Cracking of hydrocarbons produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Larger molecules", "B. Smaller molecules", "C. The same molecules", "D. Only alkanes"]', 'B', 'Cracking breaks larger hydrocarbons into smaller, more useful ones.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Polymerization of ethene produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Polystyrene", "B. Polyethene (polyethylene)", "C. PVC", "D. Nylon"]', 'B', 'Ethene monomers join to form polyethene.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Carboxylic acids have the functional group:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. -OH", "B. -CHO", "C. -COOH", "D. -CO-"]', 'C', 'Carboxylic acids contain the -COOH group.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Esterification is a reaction between:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Acid and base", "B. Alcohol and carboxylic acid", "C. Two alcohols", "D. Two acids"]', 'B', 'Ester = Alcohol + Carboxylic acid (with loss of water).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The Contact Process is used to manufacture:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ammonia", "B. Nitric acid", "C. Sulfuric acid", "D. Hydrochloric acid"]', 'C', 'The Contact Process produces sulfuric acid industrially.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'The Haber Process produces:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ammonia", "B. Sulfuric acid", "C. Nitric acid", "D. Chlorine"]', 'A', 'Haber Process: N₂ + 3H₂ ⇌ 2NH₃ (ammonia synthesis).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Acid rain is caused mainly by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Carbon dioxide only", "B. Sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides", "C. Oxygen", "D. Water vapor"]', 'B', 'SO₂ and NOₓ dissolve in rainwater to form acids.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Hard water contains compounds of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sodium and potassium", "B. Calcium and magnesium", "C. Iron and zinc", "D. Lead and copper"]', 'B', 'Hard water contains dissolved calcium and magnesium salts.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_2024_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_chemistry', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_chem_2024_1', 'Chlorination of water is done to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Soften the water", "B. Remove odor", "C. Kill microorganisms", "D. Add minerals"]', 'C', 'Chlorine disinfects water by killing harmful microorganisms.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_elec_001', 'topic_electrochemistry', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Electrolysis is the process of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Using electricity to cause a chemical reaction","Producing electricity from chemicals","Mixing acids and bases","Heating substances"]', 'Using electricity to cause a chemical reaction', 'Electrolysis uses electrical energy to drive non-spontaneous chemical reactions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_elec_002', 'topic_electrochemistry', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In electrolysis, oxidation occurs at the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Cathode","Anode","Both electrodes","Neither electrode"]', 'B', 'Oxidation (loss of electrons) occurs at the anode; reduction occurs at the cathode.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_elec_003', 'topic_electrochemistry', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A galvanic cell converts:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Electrical to chemical energy","Chemical to electrical energy","Heat to electrical energy","Light to electrical energy"]', 'B', 'A galvanic (voltaic) cell converts chemical energy into electrical energy through spontaneous reactions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_elec_004', 'topic_electrochemistry', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The electrode where reduction occurs is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Anode","Cathode","Salt bridge","Electrolyte"]', 'B', 'Reduction (gain of electrons) always occurs at the cathode.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_elec_005', 'topic_electrochemistry', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Electroplating is used to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Generate electricity","Coat metals with a thin layer of another metal","Produce hydrogen gas","Neutralize acids"]', 'B', 'Electroplating deposits a thin layer of metal onto objects for protection or decoration.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_eq_002', 'topic_equilibrium', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Le Chatelier''s principle states that a system at equilibrium will:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Stop reacting","Shift to oppose any change","Always favor products","Always favor reactants"]', 'Shift to oppose any change', 'Le Chatelier''s principle: a system will shift to counteract any stress applied to it.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_eq_003', 'topic_equilibrium', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'At equilibrium, the rate of forward reaction:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Is zero","Equals the rate of reverse reaction","Is greater than reverse","Is less than reverse"]', 'Equals the rate of reverse reaction', 'At equilibrium, forward and reverse reaction rates are equal (dynamic equilibrium).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_eq_004', 'topic_equilibrium', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Increasing pressure favors the side with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["More moles of gas","Fewer moles of gas","More solid","No effect"]', 'Fewer moles of gas', 'Increased pressure shifts equilibrium toward the side with fewer gas molecules.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_chem_eq_005', 'topic_equilibrium', 'subj_wassce_chemistry', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A catalyst in an equilibrium reaction:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Shifts equilibrium right","Shifts equilibrium left","Speeds up reaching equilibrium","Changes the equilibrium constant"]', 'Speeds up reaching equilibrium', 'A catalyst speeds up both forward and reverse reactions equally, reaching equilibrium faster.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_001', 'topic_crs_creation', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'According to Genesis, on which day did God create man?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Fifth day","Sixth day","Seventh day","Fourth day"]', 'Sixth day', 'According to Genesis 1:26-31, God created man on the sixth day of creation.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_002', 'topic_crs_patriarchs', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'God changed Abram''s name to Abraham, which means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Father of nations","Friend of God","Blessed one","Man of faith"]', 'Father of nations', 'In Genesis 17:5, God changed Abram''s name to Abraham, meaning "father of many nations" as a sign of the covenant.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_003', 'topic_crs_moses', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Ten Commandments were given to Moses at:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Mount Carmel","Mount Sinai","Mount Zion","Mount Moriah"]', 'Mount Sinai', 'God gave Moses the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai (also called Mount Horeb) as recorded in Exodus 20.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_004', 'topic_crs_jesus', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Jesus was born in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Jerusalem","Nazareth","Bethlehem","Capernaum"]', 'C', 'According to Matthew 2:1 and Luke 2:4-7, Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_005', 'topic_crs_parables', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Parable of the Good Samaritan teaches about:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Prayer","Love for neighbor","Forgiveness","Faith"]', 'Love for neighbor', 'The Parable of the Good Samaritan (Luke 10:25-37) teaches about showing compassion and love to all people, regardless of social or ethnic differences.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'In the beginning, God created:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Man and woman", "B. The heavens and the earth", "C. Light and darkness", "D. Plants and animals"]', 'B', 'Genesis 1:1 states "In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth."', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Man was created from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Water", "B. Fire", "C. Dust of the ground", "D. Air"]', 'C', 'According to Genesis 2:7, God formed man from the dust of the ground and breathed life into his nostrils.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The tree that Adam and Eve were forbidden to eat from was called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Tree of Life", "B. Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil", "C. Tree of Wisdom", "D. Tree of Paradise"]', 'B', 'God forbade Adam and Eve from eating from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil (Genesis 2:17).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The serpent was cursed to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Fly in the air", "B. Crawl on its belly", "C. Live in water", "D. Lose its scales"]', 'B', 'As punishment for deceiving Eve, the serpent was cursed to crawl on its belly and eat dust (Genesis 3:14).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'What did God place at the east of the Garden of Eden after expelling Adam and Eve?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Angels with swords", "B. Cherubim with a flaming sword", "C. A wall of fire", "D. A river"]', 'B', 'God placed cherubim with a flaming sword to guard the way to the Tree of Life (Genesis 3:24).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Abel was a:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Farmer", "B. Shepherd", "C. Hunter", "D. Builder"]', 'B', 'Abel was a keeper of sheep (shepherd) while his brother Cain was a tiller of the ground (Genesis 4:2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'What mark did God put on Cain?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A mark of death", "B. A mark of protection", "C. A mark of slavery", "D. A mark of honor"]', 'B', 'God put a protective mark on Cain so that no one who found him would kill him (Genesis 4:15).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who walked with God and was taken to heaven without dying?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Noah", "B. Enoch", "C. Abraham", "D. Moses"]', 'B', 'Enoch walked faithfully with God, and God took him away so that he did not experience death (Genesis 5:24, Hebrews 11:5).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'How many of each clean animal did Noah take into the ark?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Two", "B. Seven", "C. Twelve", "D. Fourteen"]', 'B', 'Noah was instructed to take seven pairs of every clean animal and one pair of every unclean animal (Genesis 7:2).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'What did Noah send out first to check if the waters had receded?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A dove", "B. A raven", "C. A sparrow", "D. An eagle"]', 'B', 'Noah first sent out a raven, then later sent out a dove (Genesis 8:7-8).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'God called Abraham from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Egypt", "B. Canaan", "C. Ur of the Chaldees", "D. Babylon"]', 'C', 'God called Abraham (then Abram) from Ur of the Chaldees to go to a land He would show him (Genesis 11:31, Acts 7:2-4).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The sign of God''s covenant with Abraham was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Rainbow", "B. Circumcision", "C. Sabbath", "D. Baptism"]', 'B', 'Circumcision was the sign of the covenant between God and Abraham and his descendants (Genesis 17:10-11).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Abraham''s wife Sarah gave birth to Isaac when she was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 70 years old", "B. 80 years old", "C. 90 years old", "D. 100 years old"]', 'C', 'Sarah gave birth to Isaac when she was 90 years old, as God had promised (Genesis 17:17, 21:2-5).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Isaac''s wife was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Rachel", "B. Leah", "C. Rebekah", "D. Sarah"]', 'C', 'Rebekah was Isaac''s wife, found for him by Abraham''s servant at a well (Genesis 24).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Jacob''s name was changed to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Abraham", "B. Isaac", "C. Israel", "D. Joseph"]', 'C', 'After wrestling with the angel, Jacob''s name was changed to Israel, meaning "he who struggles with God" (Genesis 32:28).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'How many sons did Jacob have?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ten", "B. Twelve", "C. Fourteen", "D. Sixteen"]', 'B', 'Jacob had twelve sons who became the ancestors of the twelve tribes of Israel.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Joseph interpreted Pharaoh''s dream about:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ten plagues", "B. Seven years of plenty and seven years of famine", "C. The Exodus", "D. A great war"]', 'B', 'Joseph interpreted Pharaoh''s dreams as meaning seven years of abundance followed by seven years of severe famine (Genesis 41:25-32).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Where did the Israelites live in Egypt?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Canaan", "B. Goshen", "C. Sinai", "D. Memphis"]', 'B', 'The Israelites settled in the land of Goshen in Egypt (Genesis 47:6).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who found baby Moses in the Nile River?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A slave girl", "B. Pharaoh''s daughter", "C. Moses'' mother", "D. Miriam"]', 'B', 'Pharaoh''s daughter found baby Moses among the reeds of the Nile and adopted him (Exodus 2:5-10).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'God appeared to Moses in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A burning bush", "B. A cloud", "C. A dream", "D. A temple"]', 'A', 'God appeared to Moses in a burning bush that was not consumed by fire at Mount Horeb (Exodus 3:2-4).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The last of the ten plagues was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Locusts", "B. Darkness", "C. Death of firstborn", "D. Boils"]', 'C', 'The tenth and final plague was the death of all firstborn in Egypt who were not protected by the lamb''s blood (Exodus 12:29).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'What did God use to guide the Israelites by day?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A pillar of fire", "B. A pillar of cloud", "C. An angel", "D. A star"]', 'B', 'God led the Israelites by a pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night (Exodus 13:21-22).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'What food did God provide for the Israelites in the wilderness?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Fish", "B. Bread only", "C. Manna and quail", "D. Fruits"]', 'C', 'God provided manna (bread from heaven) each morning and quail for meat in the evening (Exodus 16).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The first commandment states:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. You shall not kill", "B. You shall not steal", "C. You shall have no other gods before me", "D. Honor your father and mother"]', 'C', 'The first commandment is "You shall have no other gods before me" (Exodus 20:3).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The fourth commandment requires:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Not to kill", "B. Not to steal", "C. To keep the Sabbath holy", "D. To honor parents"]', 'C', 'The fourth commandment states "Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy" (Exodus 20:8).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The Ark of the Covenant contained all EXCEPT:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The tablets of the Ten Commandments", "B. Aaron''s rod that budded", "C. A pot of manna", "D. The bronze serpent"]', 'D', 'The Ark contained the tablets of the commandments, Aaron''s rod, and a pot of manna (Hebrews 9:4). The bronze serpent was made separately.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who led the Israelites across the Jordan into the Promised Land?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Moses", "B. Aaron", "C. Joshua", "D. Caleb"]', 'C', 'Joshua succeeded Moses and led the Israelites across the Jordan River into Canaan (Joshua 3).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The walls of Jericho fell after the Israelites:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Attacked with weapons", "B. Used battering rams", "C. Marched around and shouted", "D. Prayed for seven days"]', 'C', 'The walls of Jericho fell after the Israelites marched around the city for seven days and shouted (Joshua 6).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Which judge defeated the Midianites with only 300 men?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Samson", "B. Gideon", "C. Deborah", "D. Jephthah"]', 'B', 'Gideon defeated the Midianites with only 300 men using torches and trumpets (Judges 7).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who was the only female judge mentioned in the Bible?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ruth", "B. Deborah", "C. Esther", "D. Hannah"]', 'B', 'Deborah was the only female judge in Israel, who led alongside Barak (Judges 4-5).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Samuel was dedicated to God''s service by his mother:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sarah", "B. Hannah", "C. Rachel", "D. Rebekah"]', 'B', 'Hannah dedicated Samuel to God''s service at the tabernacle in Shiloh after God answered her prayer for a son (1 Samuel 1).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'King Saul disobeyed God by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Taking a census", "B. Committing adultery", "C. Sparing King Agag and the best animals", "D. Building a temple"]', 'C', 'Saul disobeyed God by not completely destroying the Amalekites; he spared King Agag and the best livestock (1 Samuel 15).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'David was the son of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Saul", "B. Jesse", "C. Samuel", "D. Jonathan"]', 'B', 'David was the son of Jesse of Bethlehem, the youngest of eight brothers (1 Samuel 16:10-11).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who was David''s best friend?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Solomon", "B. Absalom", "C. Jonathan", "D. Nathan"]', 'C', 'Jonathan, son of King Saul, was David''s closest friend. They made a covenant of friendship (1 Samuel 18:1-4).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Solomon built the first temple in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Bethlehem", "B. Nazareth", "C. Jerusalem", "D. Hebron"]', 'C', 'Solomon built the first temple of the Lord in Jerusalem on Mount Moriah (2 Chronicles 3:1).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The wicked queen who promoted Baal worship in Israel was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Esther", "B. Jezebel", "C. Athaliah", "D. Bathsheba"]', 'B', 'Jezebel, wife of King Ahab, promoted Baal worship and persecuted the prophets of God (1 Kings 16:31, 18:4).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Naaman was healed of leprosy by washing in the River:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Nile", "B. Euphrates", "C. Jordan", "D. Tigris"]', 'C', 'Elisha told Naaman to wash seven times in the Jordan River, and he was healed of leprosy (2 Kings 5:10-14).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Which empire conquered Judah and destroyed the temple?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Assyria", "B. Babylon", "C. Persia", "D. Greece"]', 'B', 'The Babylonian Empire under Nebuchadnezzar conquered Judah in 586 BC and destroyed Solomon''s temple (2 Kings 25).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Ezra was a:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. King", "B. Priest and scribe", "C. Prophet", "D. Judge"]', 'B', 'Ezra was a priest and scribe who led a group of exiles back to Jerusalem and taught the law (Ezra 7:6, 10).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Who rebuilt the walls of Jerusalem?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ezra", "B. Nehemiah", "C. Zerubbabel", "D. Haggai"]', 'B', 'Nehemiah led the project to rebuild the walls of Jerusalem in 52 days (Nehemiah 6:15).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The angel who announced Jesus'' birth to Mary was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Michael", "B. Gabriel", "C. Raphael", "D. Uriel"]', 'B', 'The angel Gabriel was sent by God to announce to Mary that she would conceive and bear a son (Luke 1:26-31).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The wise men from the East brought gifts of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gold, silver, and bronze", "B. Gold, frankincense, and myrrh", "C. Wheat, wine, and oil", "D. Sheep, goats, and cattle"]', 'B', 'The wise men brought gifts of gold, frankincense, and myrrh to the child Jesus (Matthew 2:11).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Where was Jesus when He was twelve years old and His parents found Him teaching?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The synagogue in Nazareth", "B. The temple in Jerusalem", "C. By the Sea of Galilee", "D. In Bethlehem"]', 'B', 'Jesus'' parents found Him in the temple in Jerusalem, sitting among the teachers (Luke 2:41-50).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Jesus called Peter and Andrew while they were:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Collecting taxes", "B. Fishing", "C. Building boats", "D. Shepherding"]', 'B', 'Jesus called Peter and Andrew while they were fishing, telling them He would make them fishers of men (Matthew 4:18-19).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'In the Parable of the Good Samaritan, who passed by the injured man first?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A Samaritan", "B. A priest", "C. A tax collector", "D. A soldier"]', 'B', 'A priest first passed by on the other side, then a Levite, before the Samaritan helped (Luke 10:31-33).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The Lord''s Prayer begins with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Give us this day our daily bread", "B. Our Father who art in heaven", "C. Forgive us our debts", "D. Lead us not into temptation"]', 'B', 'The Lord''s Prayer begins with "Our Father who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name" (Matthew 6:9).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Which disciple denied Jesus three times?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. John", "B. James", "C. Peter", "D. Thomas"]', 'C', 'Peter denied knowing Jesus three times before the rooster crowed, as Jesus had predicted (Matthew 26:69-75).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'Jesus rose from the dead on the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. First day", "B. Second day", "C. Third day", "D. Fourth day"]', 'C', 'Jesus rose from the dead on the third day, as He had foretold (Matthew 16:21, 1 Corinthians 15:4).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The Great Commission commands believers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Build churches", "B. Collect tithes", "C. Make disciples of all nations", "D. Observe the Sabbath"]', 'C', 'The Great Commission commands believers to go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing and teaching them (Matthew 28:19-20).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2023_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2023_1', 'The first Christian martyr was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Peter", "B. Paul", "C. Stephen", "D. James"]', 'C', 'Stephen was the first Christian martyr, stoned to death for his faith (Acts 7:54-60).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'According to the Book of Genesis, on which day did God create man?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Fourth day", "B. Fifth day", "C. Sixth day", "D. Seventh day"]', 'C', 'According to Genesis 1:26-27, God created man on the sixth day of creation, after creating animals and before resting on the seventh day.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'What was the name of the garden where Adam and Eve were placed?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Garden of Gethsemane", "B. Garden of Eden", "C. Garden of Paradise", "D. Garden of Galilee"]', 'B', 'According to Genesis 2:8, God planted a garden in Eden and placed Adam there. Eden means "delight" or "pleasure."', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Which of the following was NOT a consequence of the Fall of Man?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Death entered the world", "B. Painful childbirth for women", "C. Man would live forever", "D. Man would work hard for food"]', 'C', 'The Fall resulted in mortality, not immortality. Man was expelled from Eden to prevent him from eating from the Tree of Life and living forever (Genesis 3:22-24).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who was the first murderer mentioned in the Bible?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Abel", "B. Seth", "C. Cain", "D. Lamech"]', 'C', 'Cain killed his brother Abel out of jealousy when God accepted Abel''s offering but rejected Cain''s (Genesis 4:8).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'According to Genesis, how old was Noah when the flood came?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 500 years", "B. 600 years", "C. 700 years", "D. 800 years"]', 'B', 'Genesis 7:6 states that Noah was 600 years old when the floodwaters came upon the earth.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'What was the sign of the covenant between God and Noah?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Circumcision", "B. Rainbow", "C. Dove", "D. Olive branch"]', 'B', 'The rainbow was the sign of God''s covenant with Noah, promising never again to destroy the earth with a flood (Genesis 9:12-17).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Tower of Babel incident resulted in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A great flood", "B. Confusion of languages", "C. Death of the builders", "D. An earthquake"]', 'B', 'God confused the language of the people building the Tower of Babel, causing them to scatter across the earth (Genesis 11:7-9).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'What was the original name of Abraham?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Adam", "B. Abram", "C. Isaac", "D. Jacob"]', 'B', 'Abraham was originally named Abram. God changed his name to Abraham, meaning "father of many nations" (Genesis 17:5).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'God tested Abraham''s faith by asking him to sacrifice:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ishmael", "B. Isaac", "C. A lamb", "D. His wife"]', 'B', 'God tested Abraham by asking him to sacrifice his son Isaac on Mount Moriah (Genesis 22). God provided a ram as a substitute.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who sold his birthright for a bowl of stew?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Jacob", "B. Esau", "C. Joseph", "D. Reuben"]', 'B', 'Esau sold his birthright to his younger brother Jacob for a bowl of red lentil stew (Genesis 25:29-34).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Joseph was sold into slavery by his brothers for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ten pieces of silver", "B. Twenty pieces of silver", "C. Thirty pieces of silver", "D. Forty pieces of silver"]', 'B', 'Joseph''s brothers sold him to Midianite merchants for twenty pieces of silver (Genesis 37:28).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'What was Moses'' offense that prevented him from entering the Promised Land?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Making a golden calf", "B. Striking the rock instead of speaking to it", "C. Marrying a foreigner", "D. Killing an Egyptian"]', 'B', 'God told Moses to speak to the rock, but Moses struck it twice in anger, showing distrust in God''s word (Numbers 20:8-12).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'How many plagues did God send upon Egypt?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Seven", "B. Eight", "C. Ten", "D. Twelve"]', 'C', 'God sent ten plagues upon Egypt to compel Pharaoh to release the Israelites from slavery (Exodus 7-12).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Passover commemorates:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The crossing of the Red Sea", "B. The death angel passing over Israelite homes", "C. The giving of the Ten Commandments", "D. The manna in the wilderness"]', 'B', 'The Passover commemorates the night when the death angel passed over Israelite homes marked with lamb''s blood, sparing their firstborn (Exodus 12).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Ten Commandments were given to Moses on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mount Carmel", "B. Mount Sinai", "C. Mount of Olives", "D. Mount Zion"]', 'B', 'God gave Moses the Ten Commandments on Mount Sinai (Exodus 19-20).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Which commandment states "You shall not commit adultery"?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Fifth Commandment", "B. Sixth Commandment", "C. Seventh Commandment", "D. Eighth Commandment"]', 'C', 'The Seventh Commandment prohibits adultery (Exodus 20:14).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'While Moses was on Mount Sinai, the Israelites made:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A golden calf", "B. A bronze serpent", "C. A golden temple", "D. A silver chariot"]', 'A', 'While Moses was receiving the commandments, Aaron made a golden calf idol for the Israelites to worship (Exodus 32).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'How many spies did Moses send to explore Canaan?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ten", "B. Twelve", "C. Fourteen", "D. Sixteen"]', 'B', 'Moses sent twelve spies, one from each tribe of Israel, to explore the land of Canaan (Numbers 13:1-2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Which two spies brought a positive report about Canaan?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Moses and Aaron", "B. Joshua and Caleb", "C. Abraham and Isaac", "D. David and Jonathan"]', 'B', 'Only Joshua and Caleb believed Israel could conquer Canaan with God''s help, while the other ten spies were fearful (Numbers 14:6-9).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Israelites wandered in the wilderness for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 10 years", "B. 20 years", "C. 40 years", "D. 50 years"]', 'C', 'Due to their unbelief, the Israelites wandered in the wilderness for 40 years until that generation died out (Numbers 14:33-34).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who was the last judge of Israel before the monarchy?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gideon", "B. Samson", "C. Samuel", "D. Eli"]', 'C', 'Samuel was the last judge who also anointed the first two kings of Israel, Saul and David.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'What was the source of Samson''s strength?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. His muscles", "B. His hair", "C. His diet", "D. His armor"]', 'B', 'Samson''s strength came from his Nazirite vow, symbolized by his uncut hair. When Delilah cut it, his strength left him (Judges 16).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who was the first king of Israel?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. David", "B. Solomon", "C. Saul", "D. Samuel"]', 'C', 'Saul was the first king of Israel, anointed by Samuel at the people''s request (1 Samuel 9-10).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_crs_2024_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'David killed the giant Goliath with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A sword", "B. A spear", "C. A sling and stone", "D. A bow and arrow"]', 'C', 'David killed Goliath with a sling and a single stone, which struck the giant on the forehead (1 Samuel 17:49-50).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Which prophet confronted David about his sin with Bathsheba?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Elijah", "B. Elisha", "C. Nathan", "D. Isaiah"]', 'C', 'Prophet Nathan confronted King David with a parable about a rich man stealing a poor man''s lamb (2 Samuel 12).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Solomon asked God for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Long life", "B. Great wealth", "C. Victory over enemies", "D. Wisdom to lead Israel"]', 'D', 'When God offered Solomon anything, he asked for wisdom to govern the people. God was pleased and gave him wisdom plus riches and honor (1 Kings 3:9-13).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The kingdom of Israel divided after the death of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. David", "B. Solomon", "C. Rehoboam", "D. Jeroboam"]', 'B', 'After Solomon''s death, his son Rehoboam''s harsh rule caused the kingdom to split into Israel (North) and Judah (South) (1 Kings 12).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Elijah challenged the prophets of Baal on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mount Sinai", "B. Mount Carmel", "C. Mount Zion", "D. Mount Hermon"]', 'B', 'Elijah challenged and defeated the prophets of Baal in a dramatic contest on Mount Carmel (1 Kings 18).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'How did Elijah leave the earth?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. He died of old age", "B. He was killed by enemies", "C. He was taken up in a whirlwind", "D. He drowned in the Jordan"]', 'C', 'Elijah was taken up to heaven in a whirlwind with a chariot and horses of fire (2 Kings 2:11).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who succeeded Elijah as prophet?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Isaiah", "B. Jeremiah", "C. Elisha", "D. Amos"]', 'C', 'Elisha, who had served as Elijah''s attendant, received a double portion of his spirit and continued his prophetic ministry (2 Kings 2:9-15).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Which empire conquered the Northern Kingdom of Israel?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Babylon", "B. Assyria", "C. Persia", "D. Egypt"]', 'B', 'The Assyrian Empire conquered the Northern Kingdom of Israel in 722 BC and deported its people (2 Kings 17).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The prophet who spent three days in the belly of a great fish was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Jeremiah", "B. Jonah", "C. Joel", "D. Amos"]', 'B', 'Jonah was swallowed by a great fish for three days when he tried to flee from God''s command to preach to Nineveh (Jonah 1-2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Isaiah prophesied that the Messiah would be born of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A princess", "B. A virgin", "C. A prophet", "D. A widow"]', 'B', 'Isaiah 7:14 prophesied that a virgin would conceive and bear a son called Immanuel, fulfilled in Jesus Christ.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Daniel was thrown into the lions'' den for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Stealing from the king", "B. Praying to God", "C. Plotting against Babylon", "D. Refusing to work"]', 'B', 'Daniel was thrown into the lions'' den because he continued praying to God despite a decree forbidding prayer to anyone except King Darius (Daniel 6).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The three Hebrew boys who were thrown into the fiery furnace were:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Peter, James, and John", "B. Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego", "C. Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob", "D. David, Solomon, and Rehoboam"]', 'B', 'Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego refused to worship Nebuchadnezzar''s golden image and were thrown into a fiery furnace (Daniel 3).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Jesus was born in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Nazareth", "B. Jerusalem", "C. Bethlehem", "D. Galilee"]', 'C', 'Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea, as prophesied by Micah and recorded in Matthew 2:1 and Luke 2:4-7.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who baptized Jesus in the River Jordan?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Peter", "B. Andrew", "C. John the Baptist", "D. James"]', 'C', 'John the Baptist baptized Jesus in the River Jordan, where the Spirit descended like a dove and God''s voice confirmed Jesus as His Son (Matthew 3:13-17).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Jesus fasted in the wilderness for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Seven days", "B. Fourteen days", "C. Thirty days", "D. Forty days"]', 'D', 'Jesus fasted for forty days and nights in the wilderness before being tempted by Satan (Matthew 4:1-2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Jesus'' first miracle was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Healing a blind man", "B. Feeding 5000", "C. Turning water into wine", "D. Walking on water"]', 'C', 'Jesus'' first miracle was turning water into wine at a wedding in Cana of Galilee (John 2:1-11).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'How many disciples did Jesus choose?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ten", "B. Twelve", "C. Fourteen", "D. Sixteen"]', 'B', 'Jesus chose twelve disciples (apostles) to follow him and continue his ministry (Matthew 10:1-4).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Beatitudes are found in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The Lord''s Prayer", "B. The Sermon on the Mount", "C. The Last Supper", "D. The Parable of the Sower"]', 'B', 'The Beatitudes are the opening statements of Jesus'' Sermon on the Mount (Matthew 5:3-12).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'In the Parable of the Prodigal Son, the younger son wasted his inheritance on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Building a house", "B. Wild living", "C. Buying sheep", "D. Helping the poor"]', 'B', 'The younger son squandered his wealth on wild living before returning home repentant (Luke 15:13).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Jesus raised Lazarus from the dead after how many days?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. One day", "B. Two days", "C. Three days", "D. Four days"]', 'D', 'Lazarus had been in the tomb for four days when Jesus raised him from the dead (John 11:17, 39).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who betrayed Jesus to the Jewish authorities?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Peter", "B. Thomas", "C. Judas Iscariot", "D. Matthew"]', 'C', 'Judas Iscariot betrayed Jesus for thirty pieces of silver (Matthew 26:14-16, 47-50).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Jesus was crucified at a place called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Gethsemane", "B. Bethany", "C. Golgotha", "D. Bethlehem"]', 'C', 'Jesus was crucified at Golgotha, which means "Place of the Skull" (Matthew 27:33, John 19:17).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The Holy Spirit came upon the disciples on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Easter", "B. Passover", "C. Pentecost", "D. Christmas"]', 'C', 'The Holy Spirit came upon the disciples on the day of Pentecost, fifty days after Passover (Acts 2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Who was known as the "Apostle to the Gentiles"?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Peter", "B. James", "C. Paul", "D. John"]', 'C', 'Paul (formerly Saul) was called the Apostle to the Gentiles because of his missionary work among non-Jews (Romans 11:13).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'Saul was converted on the road to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Jerusalem", "B. Damascus", "C. Rome", "D. Athens"]', 'B', 'Saul was traveling to Damascus to persecute Christians when Jesus appeared to him and he was converted (Acts 9:1-9).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'According to Paul, the greatest of faith, hope, and love is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Faith", "B. Hope", "C. Love", "D. All are equal"]', 'C', 'In 1 Corinthians 13:13, Paul states that the greatest of these three virtues is love (charity).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_2024_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_crs', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_crs_2024_1', 'The fruits of the Spirit include all EXCEPT:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Love and joy", "B. Peace and patience", "C. Anger and jealousy", "D. Self-control and gentleness"]', 'C', 'The fruits of the Spirit in Galatians 5:22-23 are love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control. Anger and jealousy are works of the flesh.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_church_001', 'topic_crs_church', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Holy Spirit came upon the disciples at:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Christmas","Easter","Pentecost","Passover"]', 'Pentecost', 'The Holy Spirit descended on the disciples at Pentecost (Acts 2).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_church_002', 'topic_crs_church', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The first Christian martyr was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Peter","Paul","Stephen","James"]', 'Stephen', 'Stephen was stoned to death, becoming the first Christian martyr (Acts 7).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_church_003', 'topic_crs_church', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Saul of Tarsus was converted on the road to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Jerusalem","Damascus","Rome","Athens"]', 'B', 'Saul (later Paul) encountered Jesus on the road to Damascus (Acts 9).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_church_004', 'topic_crs_church', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The apostle to the Gentiles was:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Peter","James","Paul","John"]', 'Paul', 'Paul is known as the apostle to the Gentiles, spreading Christianity beyond Judaism.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_crs_church_005', 'topic_crs_church', 'subj_wassce_crs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The early Christians were first called Christians at:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Jerusalem","Antioch","Rome","Corinth"]', 'B', 'The disciples were first called Christians in Antioch (Acts 11:26).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
