('q_eco_005', 'topic_eco_money', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Which is NOT a function of money?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Medium of exchange","Store of value","Creating inflation","Unit of account"]', 'Creating inflation', 'The functions of money are: medium of exchange, store of value, unit of account, and standard of deferred payment. Creating inflation is not a function of money.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Economics is best defined as the study of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Money and banking", "B. How society allocates scarce resources", "C. Government spending", "D. Business management"]', 'B', 'Economics studies how societies allocate limited resources to satisfy unlimited wants.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The basic economic problem arises because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Resources are unlimited", "B. Wants are limited", "C. Resources are scarce and wants are unlimited", "D. There is no government intervention"]', 'C', 'Scarcity occurs because resources are limited while human wants are unlimited.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Opportunity cost is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The total cost of production", "B. The money spent on goods", "C. The next best alternative forgone", "D. The cost of raw materials"]', 'C', 'Opportunity cost is the value of the next best alternative that is sacrificed when making a choice.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The Production Possibility Frontier (PPF) shows:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Consumer preferences", "B. Maximum output combinations with given resources", "C. Import and export balance", "D. Government budget"]', 'B', 'The PPF shows the maximum combinations of goods that can be produced with available resources.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Which is NOT a factor of production?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Land", "B. Labor", "C. Money", "D. Capital"]', 'C', 'The factors of production are land, labor, capital, and entrepreneurship. Money is a medium of exchange.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Division of labor refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sharing profits", "B. Splitting work into specialized tasks", "C. Dividing land", "D. Separating capital"]', 'B', 'Division of labor involves breaking down production into specialized tasks performed by different workers.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A mixed economy is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only private ownership", "B. Only government ownership", "C. Both private and public sector participation", "D. No economic planning"]', 'C', 'A mixed economy combines elements of both market and command economies.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Capital goods are used to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Satisfy immediate wants", "B. Produce other goods", "C. Export only", "D. Pay wages"]', 'B', 'Capital goods are used in the production of other goods and services.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The reward for entrepreneurship is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Wages", "B. Rent", "C. Interest", "D. Profit"]', 'D', 'Entrepreneurs receive profit as the reward for risk-taking and organizing production.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Normative economics deals with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Facts and data", "B. What ought to be", "C. Historical trends", "D. Statistical analysis"]', 'B', 'Normative economics involves value judgments about what economic policies ought to be.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The law of demand states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Price and quantity demanded move together", "B. Higher prices lead to lower quantity demanded, ceteris paribus", "C. Supply creates its own demand", "D. Demand is constant"]', 'B', 'The law of demand: as price rises, quantity demanded falls, all other things being equal.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A movement along the demand curve is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Change in income", "B. Change in tastes", "C. Change in price of the good", "D. Change in population"]', 'C', 'A movement along the curve is caused by a change in the price of the good itself.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'If demand is price inelastic, a price increase will:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Decrease total revenue", "B. Increase total revenue", "C. Not affect total revenue", "D. Double the quantity demanded"]', 'B', 'With inelastic demand, price increases lead to higher total revenue as quantity falls proportionally less.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Complementary goods are goods that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Can substitute for each other", "B. Are used together", "C. Are luxury items", "D. Have no relation"]', 'B', 'Complementary goods are consumed together, like cars and fuel.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The equilibrium price is determined where:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Demand exceeds supply", "B. Supply exceeds demand", "C. Demand equals supply", "D. Price is highest"]', 'C', 'Equilibrium price occurs where quantity demanded equals quantity supplied.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A price ceiling set below equilibrium will cause:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Surplus", "B. Shortage", "C. Equilibrium", "D. Increased production"]', 'B', 'A price ceiling below equilibrium creates shortage as quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Cross elasticity of demand measures responsiveness of demand to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Income changes", "B. Price changes of related goods", "C. Own price changes", "D. Supply changes"]', 'B', 'Cross elasticity measures how demand for one good responds to price changes of another good.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Normal goods have:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Negative income elasticity", "B. Zero income elasticity", "C. Positive income elasticity", "D. Infinite income elasticity"]', 'C', 'Normal goods have positive income elasticity - demand increases as income rises.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A rightward shift in the supply curve indicates:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Decrease in supply", "B. Increase in supply", "C. Movement along the curve", "D. Change in demand"]', 'B', 'A rightward shift means more is supplied at every price level - an increase in supply.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Price elasticity of supply is likely to be higher when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Time period is short", "B. Time period is long", "C. Resources are fixed", "D. Technology is outdated"]', 'B', 'Supply is more elastic over longer time periods as producers can adjust capacity.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Perfect competition is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Few sellers", "B. Many buyers and sellers with homogeneous products", "C. Product differentiation", "D. Barriers to entry"]', 'B', 'Perfect competition has many firms, identical products, and free entry/exit.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A monopoly exists when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. There are many sellers", "B. There is only one seller", "C. Products are identical", "D. Entry is free"]', 'B', 'A monopoly has a single seller controlling the entire market.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Oligopoly is a market structure with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. One seller", "B. Many sellers", "C. Few dominant sellers", "D. Perfect competition"]', 'C', 'Oligopoly has few large firms that dominate the market.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Monopolistic competition differs from perfect competition because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. There are fewer firms", "B. Products are differentiated", "C. There is only one firm", "D. Prices are fixed by government"]', 'B', 'Monopolistic competition has many firms but with differentiated products.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A cartel is formed when firms:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Compete aggressively", "B. Agree to fix prices or output", "C. Lower prices", "D. Exit the market"]', 'B', 'A cartel is a formal agreement among firms to coordinate prices or production.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'In perfect competition, firms are price:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Makers", "B. Takers", "C. Setters", "D. Controllers"]', 'B', 'In perfect competition, individual firms are price takers - they accept the market price.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_eco_2023_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Natural monopoly occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government grants exclusive rights", "B. One firm can supply at lowest cost", "C. There are no substitutes", "D. Demand is very high"]', 'B', 'Natural monopoly exists when one firm can supply the entire market more efficiently than multiple firms.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Price discrimination requires:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Perfect competition", "B. Market power and ability to segment markets", "C. Free entry", "D. Homogeneous products"]', 'B', 'Price discrimination requires market power and ability to prevent resale between market segments.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The functions of money include all EXCEPT:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Medium of exchange", "B. Store of value", "C. Factor of production", "D. Unit of account"]', 'C', 'Money functions as medium of exchange, store of value, unit of account, and standard of deferred payment.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The central bank of Ghana is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ghana Commercial Bank", "B. Bank of Ghana", "C. Barclays Bank", "D. Ecobank"]', 'B', 'The Bank of Ghana is the central bank of Ghana, responsible for monetary policy.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Commercial banks create money through:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Printing currency", "B. Credit creation", "C. Taxation", "D. Government grants"]', 'B', 'Commercial banks create money by making loans, which become deposits and can be lent again.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Open market operations involve:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Setting interest rates", "B. Buying and selling government securities", "C. Printing money", "D. Setting reserve requirements"]', 'B', 'Open market operations involve central bank buying or selling government securities to control money supply.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Inflation is defined as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Decrease in prices", "B. Sustained increase in general price level", "C. Increase in output", "D. Decrease in money supply"]', 'B', 'Inflation is a persistent rise in the general level of prices over time.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Cost-push inflation is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Increased demand", "B. Rising production costs", "C. Lower interest rates", "D. Government spending"]', 'B', 'Cost-push inflation occurs when rising input costs push up prices.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The exchange rate is the price of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Goods in the domestic market", "B. One currency in terms of another", "C. Government bonds", "D. Stocks and shares"]', 'B', 'Exchange rate is the rate at which one currency can be exchanged for another.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Fiscal policy involves the use of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Interest rates", "B. Government spending and taxation", "C. Money supply", "D. Exchange rates"]', 'B', 'Fiscal policy uses government spending and taxation to influence the economy.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A progressive tax is one where:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Everyone pays the same amount", "B. Tax rate increases with income", "C. Tax rate decreases with income", "D. Tax is based on wealth only"]', 'B', 'Progressive taxation means higher income earners pay a higher percentage of their income.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Public goods are characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Excludability and rivalry", "B. Non-excludability and non-rivalry", "C. High prices", "D. Private provision only"]', 'B', 'Public goods are non-excludable and non-rivalrous, like national defense.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A budget deficit occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Revenue exceeds expenditure", "B. Expenditure exceeds revenue", "C. Revenue equals expenditure", "D. There is no taxation"]', 'B', 'Budget deficit means government spending exceeds its revenue.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Externalities are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Internal costs", "B. Third-party effects not reflected in market prices", "C. Government regulations", "D. Private benefits"]', 'B', 'Externalities are costs or benefits affecting parties not directly involved in a transaction.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Privatization means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government takeover of private firms", "B. Transfer of state enterprises to private ownership", "C. Nationalization", "D. Increasing government control"]', 'B', 'Privatization involves selling state-owned enterprises to private investors.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'GDP measures:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Total imports", "B. Total value of goods and services produced", "C. Government debt", "D. Foreign investment only"]', 'B', 'GDP is the total value of all goods and services produced within a country in a given period.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Comparative advantage is based on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Absolute cost differences", "B. Relative opportunity costs", "C. Exchange rates", "D. Population size"]', 'B', 'Comparative advantage means producing goods at lower opportunity cost relative to trading partners.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A tariff is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A subsidy on exports", "B. A tax on imports", "C. A quota on production", "D. A trade agreement"]', 'B', 'A tariff is a tax imposed on imported goods.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'The balance of trade is the difference between:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Assets and liabilities", "B. Exports and imports of goods", "C. Income and expenditure", "D. Savings and investment"]', 'B', 'Balance of trade = value of exports - value of imports of goods.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'ECOWAS stands for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. East African Economic Community", "B. Economic Community of West African States", "C. European Community of Western States", "D. Economic Council of World States"]', 'B', 'ECOWAS is the Economic Community of West African States, promoting regional integration.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Dumping occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Goods are sold at low quality", "B. Goods are sold below cost in foreign markets", "C. Goods are recycled", "D. Goods are imported cheaply"]', 'B', 'Dumping is selling goods in foreign markets below production cost or domestic price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'A quota is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A tax on imports", "B. A limit on quantity of imports", "C. A type of subsidy", "D. An exchange rate"]', 'B', 'A quota is a quantitative restriction on the amount of a good that can be imported.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Currency appreciation means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Currency loses value", "B. Currency gains value against others", "C. Inflation increases", "D. Interest rates fall"]', 'B', 'Appreciation means a currency increases in value relative to other currencies.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2023_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2023_1', 'Terms of trade refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Trade agreements", "B. Ratio of export prices to import prices", "C. Trade barriers", "D. Trade balance"]', 'B', 'Terms of trade = (index of export prices / index of import prices) × 100.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Economics is best defined as the study of how:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government controls the economy", "B. Scarce resources are allocated to satisfy unlimited wants", "C. Money is created and distributed", "D. Businesses maximize profits"]', 'B', 'Economics fundamentally deals with the allocation of scarce resources to satisfy unlimited human wants.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The opportunity cost of a decision is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The total cost of the decision", "B. The money spent on the decision", "C. The value of the next best alternative forgone", "D. The profit made from the decision"]', 'C', 'Opportunity cost refers to what you give up (the next best alternative) when you make a choice.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Which of the following is NOT a factor of production?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Land", "B. Labour", "C. Money", "D. Capital"]', 'C', 'The four factors of production are Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship. Money is not a factor of production but a medium of exchange.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The reward for entrepreneurship is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Wages", "B. Rent", "C. Interest", "D. Profit"]', 'D', 'Wages reward labour, rent rewards land, interest rewards capital, and profit rewards entrepreneurship.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The production possibility curve shows:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The actual output of an economy", "B. The maximum output combinations an economy can produce", "C. The minimum output of an economy", "D. The imports and exports of a country"]', 'B', 'The PPC illustrates the maximum combinations of two goods that can be produced with available resources.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'In a free market economy, resources are allocated primarily by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government directives", "B. Price mechanism", "C. Traditional methods", "D. Central planning"]', 'B', 'In a free market economy, the price mechanism (forces of demand and supply) allocates resources.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A mixed economy is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only private ownership of resources", "B. Only government ownership of resources", "C. Both private and public sector participation", "D. No government intervention"]', 'C', 'A mixed economy combines elements of both market and planned economies, with both private and public sectors.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Scarcity in economics implies that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Goods are not available", "B. Resources are limited relative to wants", "C. There is no production", "D. Prices are too high"]', 'B', 'Scarcity means resources are limited while human wants are unlimited, forcing choices to be made.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Economic goods are different from free goods because economic goods:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Are always expensive", "B. Have opportunity cost", "C. Are made by government", "D. Are not useful"]', 'B', 'Economic goods are scarce and have opportunity cost, while free goods (like air) are abundant and have no opportunity cost.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The basic economic problem is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Unemployment", "B. Inflation", "C. Scarcity", "D. Poverty"]', 'C', 'Scarcity is the fundamental economic problem - unlimited wants vs limited resources.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The law of demand states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. As price increases, quantity demanded increases", "B. As price decreases, quantity demanded decreases", "C. As price increases, quantity demanded decreases, ceteris paribus", "D. Price and demand are not related"]', 'C', 'The law of demand shows an inverse relationship between price and quantity demanded, all other factors held constant.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A movement along a demand curve is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Change in consumer income", "B. Change in tastes and preferences", "C. Change in the price of the good itself", "D. Change in population"]', 'C', 'Movement along a demand curve is caused only by a change in the price of the good. Other factors shift the curve.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'When two goods are substitutes, an increase in the price of one will:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Decrease demand for the other", "B. Increase demand for the other", "C. Have no effect on the other", "D. Decrease supply of the other"]', 'B', 'Substitutes are goods that can replace each other. Higher price of one increases demand for the other.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Equilibrium price is determined where:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Demand exceeds supply", "B. Supply exceeds demand", "C. Demand equals supply", "D. Government sets the price"]', 'C', 'Market equilibrium occurs where quantity demanded equals quantity supplied.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Price elasticity of demand measures:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. How supply responds to price changes", "B. The responsiveness of quantity demanded to price changes", "C. The slope of the demand curve", "D. Total revenue changes"]', 'B', 'Price elasticity of demand (PED) measures how sensitive quantity demanded is to price changes.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'If demand is elastic, a decrease in price will lead to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Decrease in total revenue", "B. Increase in total revenue", "C. No change in total revenue", "D. Decrease in quantity demanded"]', 'B', 'With elastic demand (PED > 1), the percentage increase in quantity exceeds the percentage price decrease, raising total revenue.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Which of the following goods is likely to have inelastic demand?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Luxury cars", "B. Salt", "C. Designer clothes", "D. Vacations"]', 'B', 'Necessities with few substitutes (like salt) tend to have inelastic demand - quantity demanded changes little with price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A price floor set above equilibrium will result in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Shortage", "B. Surplus", "C. Equilibrium", "D. No effect"]', 'B', 'A price floor above equilibrium (like minimum wage) creates surplus as quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Consumer surplus is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The extra goods consumers buy", "B. The difference between what consumers are willing to pay and what they actually pay", "C. The profit made by sellers", "D. Unsold goods in the market"]', 'B', 'Consumer surplus represents the benefit consumers get from paying less than their maximum willingness to pay.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The law of supply states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. As price rises, quantity supplied falls", "B. As price rises, quantity supplied rises, ceteris paribus", "C. Supply and price are unrelated", "D. Higher prices reduce production"]', 'B', 'The law of supply shows a positive relationship between price and quantity supplied.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The law of diminishing marginal returns states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Output always decreases", "B. Adding more variable inputs eventually yields smaller increases in output", "C. Costs always increase", "D. Production is always inefficient"]', 'B', 'As more of a variable factor is added to fixed factors, marginal product eventually decreases.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Fixed costs are costs that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Change with output level", "B. Do not change with output level in the short run", "C. Are always zero", "D. Only occur in the long run"]', 'B', 'Fixed costs (rent, salaries) remain constant regardless of output in the short run.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Average cost is calculated as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Total cost × Output", "B. Total cost ÷ Output", "C. Marginal cost × Output", "D. Fixed cost + Variable cost"]', 'B', 'Average cost (AC) = Total cost (TC) / Quantity (Q).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Economies of scale refer to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Increasing costs as output expands", "B. Decreasing average costs as output expands", "C. Constant costs at all output levels", "D. Losses made by large firms"]', 'B', 'Economies of scale occur when average costs fall as the scale of production increases.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Division of labour refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Sharing profits among workers", "B. Breaking production into specialized tasks", "C. Dividing a company into departments", "D. Reducing the workforce"]', 'B', 'Division of labour involves breaking down production into specialized tasks performed by different workers.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The short run in economics is a period when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. All factors are variable", "B. At least one factor is fixed", "C. No production takes place", "D. Only labor is used"]', 'B', 'In the short run, at least one factor of production is fixed; in the long run, all factors are variable.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Marginal cost is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Total cost of production", "B. Average cost per unit", "C. Additional cost of producing one more unit", "D. Fixed cost of production"]', 'C', 'Marginal cost (MC) is the extra cost incurred from producing one additional unit of output.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Internal economies of scale arise from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Growth of the industry", "B. Growth of the individual firm", "C. Government subsidies", "D. Reduced taxation"]', 'B', 'Internal economies arise from the growth of the firm itself; external economies arise from industry growth.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Perfect competition is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Few sellers", "B. Product differentiation", "C. Many buyers and sellers with homogeneous products", "D. High barriers to entry"]', 'C', 'Perfect competition features many buyers and sellers, identical products, and free entry/exit.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A monopoly exists when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. There are many sellers", "B. There is only one seller in the market", "C. Products are identical", "D. Entry is free"]', 'B', 'Monopoly is a market structure with a single seller controlling the entire market supply.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Monopolistic competition differs from perfect competition because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. There are few sellers", "B. Products are differentiated", "C. There are barriers to entry", "D. Firms are price makers"]', 'B', 'Monopolistic competition has many sellers like perfect competition, but products are differentiated.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'An oligopoly market is dominated by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. One firm", "B. Two firms only", "C. A few large firms", "D. Many small firms"]', 'C', 'Oligopoly is characterized by a few dominant firms with significant market power.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Price discrimination occurs when a firm:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Charges the same price to all customers", "B. Charges different prices for the same product to different customers", "C. Reduces prices for everyone", "D. Increases quality"]', 'B', 'Price discrimination involves charging different prices to different consumers for the same product.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A cartel is an agreement among:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Consumers to buy together", "B. Firms to fix prices or output", "C. Workers to demand higher wages", "D. Government and firms"]', 'B', 'A cartel is a formal agreement among competing firms to coordinate prices, output, or market division.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'In perfect competition, firms are price takers because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government sets prices", "B. Each firm is too small to influence market price", "C. There is only one buyer", "D. Products are differentiated"]', 'B', 'In perfect competition, individual firms are too small relative to the market to affect price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Which is NOT a function of money?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Medium of exchange", "B. Store of value", "C. Factor of production", "D. Unit of account"]', 'C', 'Money functions as medium of exchange, store of value, unit of account, and standard of deferred payment - but not as a factor of production.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_037', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The central bank of Ghana is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ghana Commercial Bank", "B. Bank of Ghana", "C. Barclays Bank", "D. World Bank"]', 'B', 'The Bank of Ghana is Ghana''s central bank, responsible for monetary policy.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 37, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_038', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Commercial banks create money through:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Printing currency", "B. The credit creation process", "C. Selling gold", "D. Government grants"]', 'B', 'Commercial banks create money through the credit creation (money multiplier) process.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 38, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_039', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Inflation is defined as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A fall in prices", "B. A sustained increase in the general price level", "C. An increase in output", "D. A decrease in money supply"]', 'B', 'Inflation is a persistent rise in the general level of prices over time.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 39, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_040', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'GDP stands for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. General Domestic Product", "B. Gross Domestic Product", "C. Government Domestic Policy", "D. Gross Domestic Price"]', 'B', 'GDP (Gross Domestic Product) is the total value of goods and services produced within a country.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 40, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_041', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The multiplier effect in economics shows that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Income decreases over time", "B. An initial injection leads to a larger final increase in national income", "C. Savings always equal investment", "D. Taxes reduce spending"]', 'B', 'The multiplier shows how an initial change in spending leads to a larger change in national income.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 41, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_042', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Monetary policy involves:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government spending decisions", "B. Central bank control of money supply and interest rates", "C. Tax changes", "D. Trade restrictions"]', 'B', 'Monetary policy is the central bank''s use of interest rates and money supply to influence the economy.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 42, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_043', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Absolute advantage means a country can:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Produce everything cheaper", "B. Produce a good using fewer resources than another country", "C. Export more than it imports", "D. Have no trade barriers"]', 'B', 'Absolute advantage exists when a country can produce a good with fewer resources than another.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 43, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_044', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'A tariff is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. A subsidy on exports", "B. A tax on imports", "C. A limit on imports", "D. A ban on trade"]', 'B', 'A tariff is a tax imposed on imported goods to protect domestic industries.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 44, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_045', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The balance of trade is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Total imports plus exports", "B. The difference between visible exports and visible imports", "C. All international transactions", "D. Only service trade"]', 'B', 'Balance of trade = Value of exports of goods minus value of imports of goods.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 45, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_046', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Exchange rate is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The interest rate on loans", "B. The price of one currency in terms of another", "C. The inflation rate", "D. The tax rate on imports"]', 'B', 'Exchange rate is the rate at which one currency can be exchanged for another.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 46, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_047', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'ECOWAS stands for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Economic Community of West African States", "B. European Community of Western African States", "C. Economic Council of West African Services", "D. Eastern Community of West African States"]', 'A', 'ECOWAS is the Economic Community of West African States, a regional economic union.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 47, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_048', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Economic development differs from economic growth because development:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only measures GDP increase", "B. Includes improvements in living standards, health, and education", "C. Is easier to measure", "D. Occurs only in rich countries"]', 'B', 'Development is broader than growth, encompassing quality of life improvements, not just output increases.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 48, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'The Human Development Index (HDI) measures:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only income", "B. Income, education, and life expectancy", "C. Only population growth", "D. Trade balance"]', 'B', 'HDI combines life expectancy, education (literacy and enrollment), and income (GDP per capita).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_2024_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eco_2024_1', 'Foreign direct investment (FDI) refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Loans from foreign governments", "B. Investment by foreign companies in productive assets in another country", "C. Aid from international organizations", "D. Buying foreign currency"]', 'B', 'FDI involves establishing business operations or acquiring business assets in a foreign country.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_cost_001', 'topic_eco_costs', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Fixed costs are costs that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Change with output","Remain constant regardless of output","Are always zero","Equal variable costs"]', 'Remain constant regardless of output', 'Fixed costs (like rent, insurance) remain constant regardless of the level of output in the short run.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_cost_002', 'topic_eco_costs', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Marginal cost is the cost of producing:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["The first unit","The last unit","One more unit","All units"]', 'One more unit', 'Marginal cost is the additional cost of producing one more unit of output.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_cost_003', 'topic_eco_costs', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Average cost is calculated as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total cost × quantity","Total cost ÷ quantity","Marginal cost × quantity","Fixed cost + variable cost"]', 'Total cost ÷ quantity', 'Average cost (AC) = Total Cost / Quantity produced.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_cost_004', 'topic_eco_costs', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Total revenue is calculated as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Price × quantity sold","Price + quantity sold","Price ÷ quantity sold","Price - cost"]', 'Price × quantity sold', 'Total Revenue (TR) = Price × Quantity sold.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_cost_005', 'topic_eco_costs', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A firm makes normal profit when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["TR > TC","TR < TC","TR = TC","MR = MC"]', 'TR = TC', 'Normal profit occurs when Total Revenue equals Total Cost (TR = TC), meaning the firm covers all costs including opportunity cost.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_dem_002', 'topic_eco_demand', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An increase in consumer income will:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Decrease demand for normal goods","Increase demand for normal goods","Not affect demand","Decrease supply"]', 'Increase demand for normal goods', 'Higher income increases purchasing power, raising demand for normal goods.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_dem_003', 'topic_eco_demand', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Complementary goods are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Goods used together","Goods that replace each other","Luxury goods","Inferior goods"]', 'Goods used together', 'Complementary goods are used together (e.g., cars and petrol).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_dem_004', 'topic_eco_demand', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A surplus occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Quantity demanded exceeds quantity supplied","Quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded","Prices are at equilibrium","There is no market"]', 'Quantity supplied exceeds quantity demanded', 'A surplus (excess supply) occurs when supply exceeds demand at the current price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_dem_005', 'topic_eco_demand', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The law of supply states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Price and quantity supplied move in opposite directions","Price and quantity supplied move in the same direction","Supply is always constant","Supply equals demand"]', 'Price and quantity supplied move in the same direction', 'Law of supply: higher prices lead to higher quantity supplied (positive relationship).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_elast_002', 'topic_eco_elasticity', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Inelastic demand means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Demand is very responsive to price","Demand is not very responsive to price","Demand is constant","There is no demand"]', 'B', 'Inelastic demand shows little change in quantity demanded when price changes.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_elast_003', 'topic_eco_elasticity', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Necessities typically have:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Elastic demand","Inelastic demand","Infinite elasticity","Zero elasticity"]', 'Inelastic demand', 'Necessities have inelastic demand because people need them regardless of price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_elast_004', 'topic_eco_elasticity', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'If PED = 0.5, demand is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Elastic","Inelastic","Unit elastic","Perfectly elastic"]', 'Inelastic', 'PED < 1 indicates inelastic demand.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_elast_005', 'topic_eco_elasticity', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Cross elasticity measures responsiveness of demand to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Own price changes","Income changes","Price of related goods","Supply changes"]', 'Price of related goods', 'Cross elasticity of demand measures how demand for one good responds to price changes of another.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_intro_002', 'topic_eco_intro', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Economics studies how to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Make money","Allocate scarce resources to satisfy unlimited wants","Run a business","Manage banks"]', 'B', 'Economics is the study of how societies allocate limited resources to meet unlimited wants.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_intro_003', 'topic_eco_intro', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Microeconomics focuses on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["The whole economy","Individual markets and consumers","Government policy only","International trade only"]', 'Individual markets and consumers', 'Microeconomics studies individual economic units like households, firms, and markets.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_intro_004', 'topic_eco_intro', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A production possibility curve shows:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Maximum output combinations with available resources","Only consumer goods","Only capital goods","Unlimited production"]', 'Maximum output combinations with available resources', 'The PPC shows the maximum combinations of goods an economy can produce with its resources.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_intro_005', 'topic_eco_intro', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In a market economy, prices are determined by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["The government","Supply and demand","Producers only","Consumers only"]', 'Supply and demand', 'In a market economy, prices are determined by the interaction of supply and demand.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mkt_002', 'topic_eco_markets', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A monopoly exists when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Many firms sell identical products","One firm dominates the market","Firms compete freely","Government controls all prices"]', 'One firm dominates the market', 'A monopoly is a market structure with a single dominant seller.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mkt_003', 'topic_eco_markets', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Perfect competition has:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Few sellers","Many sellers of identical products","One seller","Two sellers"]', 'Many sellers of identical products', 'Perfect competition features many sellers offering identical (homogeneous) products.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mkt_004', 'topic_eco_markets', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An oligopoly is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Many small firms","A few large dominant firms","Only one firm","Perfect information"]', 'B', 'An oligopoly has a small number of large firms that dominate the market.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mkt_005', 'topic_eco_markets', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Monopolistic competition combines features of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Only monopoly","Only perfect competition","Both monopoly and perfect competition","Neither monopoly nor competition"]', 'C', 'Monopolistic competition has many firms (like perfect competition) with differentiated products (like monopoly power).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mon_002', 'topic_eco_money', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Fiat money has value because:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["It is backed by gold","The government declares it legal tender","It can be exchanged for silver","It is made of valuable metal"]', 'The government declares it legal tender', 'Fiat money has value by government decree, not intrinsic value or commodity backing.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mon_003', 'topic_eco_money', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The money supply includes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Only coins","Only notes","Currency in circulation and bank deposits","Only gold reserves"]', 'Currency in circulation and bank deposits', 'Money supply includes physical currency and various types of bank deposits.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mon_004', 'topic_eco_money', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'When a central bank increases interest rates:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Borrowing becomes cheaper","Borrowing becomes more expensive","Prices fall immediately","Exports increase"]', 'Borrowing becomes more expensive', 'Higher interest rates make borrowing more expensive, discouraging spending.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_mon_005', 'topic_eco_money', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Deflation means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Rising prices","Falling prices","Stable prices","Rising unemployment only"]', 'Falling prices', 'Deflation is a sustained decrease in the general price level.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_nat_001', 'topic_eco_national', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'GDP stands for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["General Domestic Product","Gross Domestic Product","Gross Development Plan","General Development Product"]', 'Gross Domestic Product', 'GDP stands for Gross Domestic Product - the total value of goods and services produced within a country.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_eco_nat_002', 'topic_eco_national', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The difference between GDP and GNP is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["There is no difference","GNP includes net income from abroad","GDP includes net income from abroad","GNP only counts manufacturing"]', 'GNP includes net income from abroad', 'GNP = GDP + Net income from abroad. GNP includes earnings of citizens abroad minus foreigners'' earnings domestically.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_nat_003', 'topic_eco_national', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The income method of measuring national income adds up:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["All expenditures","All incomes earned","All outputs produced","All imports and exports"]', 'B', 'The income method sums all incomes earned in production - wages, rent, interest, and profits.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_nat_004', 'topic_eco_national', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Per capita income is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total income","National income divided by population","Income of capital owners","Government revenue"]', 'National income divided by population', 'Per capita income = National Income / Population. It shows average income per person.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_nat_005', 'topic_eco_national', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Double counting in national income is avoided by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Using market prices","Using only final goods or value added method","Counting all goods","Including intermediate goods"]', 'Using only final goods or value added method', 'To avoid double counting, only final goods are counted, or the value added at each stage of production.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_prod_001', 'topic_eco_production', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The law of diminishing returns states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Returns always decrease","Eventually, adding more of a variable factor yields less additional output","Fixed costs always increase","Production always increases"]', 'Eventually, adding more of a variable factor yields less additional output', 'The law of diminishing returns states that adding more of a variable factor to fixed factors eventually yields diminishing marginal returns.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_prod_002', 'topic_eco_production', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The four factors of production are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Land, labor, money, enterprise","Land, labor, capital, enterprise","Land, labor, capital, government","Land, labor, capital, technology"]', 'Land, labor, capital, enterprise', 'The four factors of production are Land, Labor, Capital, and Enterprise (entrepreneurship).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_prod_003', 'topic_eco_production', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The reward for enterprise is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Wages","Rent","Interest","Profit"]', 'Profit', 'Entrepreneurs receive profit as their reward. Wages go to labor, rent to land, and interest to capital.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_prod_004', 'topic_eco_production', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Marginal product is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total output divided by inputs","Additional output from one more unit of input","Average output per worker","Maximum possible output"]', 'B', 'Marginal product is the additional output gained from employing one more unit of a variable factor.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_prod_005', 'topic_eco_production', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Division of labor leads to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Decreased productivity","Increased specialization","Higher unemployment","Lower quality"]', 'Increased specialization', 'Division of labor increases specialization, which improves efficiency and productivity.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_trade_001', 'topic_eco_trade', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A tariff is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A tax on imports","A limit on imports","A subsidy on exports","A trade agreement"]', 'A tax on imports', 'A tariff is a tax imposed on imported goods, making them more expensive than domestic goods.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_trade_002', 'topic_eco_trade', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The balance of trade measures:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total imports and exports","Difference between visible exports and imports","Total foreign investment","Government borrowing"]', 'B', 'Balance of Trade = Value of Visible Exports - Value of Visible Imports (goods only).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_trade_003', 'topic_eco_trade', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A quota is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A tax on imports","A physical limit on imports","A type of currency","An export subsidy"]', 'B', 'A quota is a quantitative restriction limiting the amount of a good that can be imported.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_trade_004', 'topic_eco_trade', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Comparative advantage means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Producing everything cheaper","Producing a good at lower opportunity cost","Having more resources","Trading with neighbors"]', 'Producing a good at lower opportunity cost', 'Comparative advantage is the ability to produce a good at a lower opportunity cost than another country.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eco_trade_005', 'topic_eco_trade', 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Devaluation of currency makes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Exports cheaper and imports expensive","Exports expensive and imports cheaper","No difference to trade","Both exports and imports cheaper"]', 'Exports cheaper and imports expensive', 'Devaluation makes exports cheaper (more competitive) and imports more expensive.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_basic_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Scarcity in economics means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["There is nothing available","Resources are limited relative to wants","Prices are too high","No one wants goods"]', 'Resources are limited relative to wants', 'Scarcity refers to the limited availability of resources relative to unlimited human wants.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_basic_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Opportunity cost is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["The price paid for goods","The next best alternative forgone","Total production cost","Money spent on advertising"]', 'The next best alternative forgone', 'Opportunity cost is the value of the best alternative given up when a choice is made.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_basic_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The factors of production are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Money, machines, materials","Land, labour, capital, enterprise","Imports and exports","Supply and demand"]', 'Land, labour, capital, enterprise', 'The four factors of production are land, labour, capital, and entrepreneurship.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_basic_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A mixed economy combines:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Only capitalism","Only socialism","Elements of both market and planned economy","Only traditional systems"]', 'Elements of both market and planned economy', 'A mixed economy has characteristics of both market (capitalism) and planned (socialism) systems.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_basic_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The basic economic problem is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["How to advertise products","What, how, and for whom to produce","How to print money","How to eliminate poverty"]', 'What, how, and for whom to produce', 'The basic economic questions are: What to produce? How to produce? For whom to produce?', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_ds_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The law of demand states that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["As price rises, quantity demanded rises","As price falls, quantity demanded rises","Price and demand are unrelated","Demand is always constant"]', 'B', 'Law of demand: price and quantity demanded are inversely related (ceteris paribus).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_ds_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A shift in the demand curve is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Change in price of the good","Change in consumer income","Change in quantity demanded","Movement along the curve"]', 'B', 'Non-price factors like income, preferences, or prices of related goods shift the curve.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_ds_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Equilibrium price occurs when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Demand exceeds supply","Supply exceeds demand","Quantity demanded equals quantity supplied","Government sets the price"]', 'Quantity demanded equals quantity supplied', 'Equilibrium is where the demand and supply curves intersect.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_ds_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'If supply increases while demand remains constant:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Price rises","Price falls","Price stays the same","Quantity decreases"]', 'Price falls', 'Increased supply with constant demand leads to lower equilibrium price.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_ds_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Price elasticity of demand measures:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Total spending","Responsiveness of demand to price changes","Supply changes","Production costs"]', 'Responsiveness of demand to price changes', 'Price elasticity measures how sensitive quantity demanded is to price changes.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_money_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Functions of money include:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Only store of value","Medium of exchange, unit of account, store of value","Only measure of debt","Only means of payment"]', 'Medium of exchange, unit of account, store of value', 'Money serves as medium of exchange, unit of account, store of value, and standard of deferred payment.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_money_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Central Bank of Ghana:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Issues currency","Gives loans to individuals","Sells consumer goods","Operates retail stores"]', 'Issues currency', 'The Central Bank (Bank of Ghana) is responsible for issuing currency and monetary policy.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_money_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Commercial banks create money through:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Printing currency","Lending and the multiplier effect","Importing gold","Selling bonds only"]', 'Lending and the multiplier effect', 'Banks create money through the lending process and credit multiplier.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_money_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Inflation refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Falling prices","Rising general price level","Stable prices","Increasing production"]', 'Rising general price level', 'Inflation is a sustained increase in the general price level over time.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_econ_money_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_economics', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Interest rate is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Price of goods","Cost of borrowing money","Tax on income","Profit margin"]', 'B', 'Interest rate is the cost of borrowing money or the return on lending.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_001', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Simplify: (27)^(2/3) × (8)^(-1/3)', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["3", "6", "9/2", "18"]', '9/2', '27^(2/3) = 9, 8^(-1/3) = 1/2. Result: 9 × 1/2 = 9/2', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_002', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'If log₁₀2 = 0.3010 and log₁₀3 = 0.4771, find log₁₀12', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["0.7781", "1.0791", "1.2041", "0.9542"]', '1.0791', 'log₁₀12 = 2log₁₀2 + log₁₀3 = 0.6020 + 0.4771 = 1.0791', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_003', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Rationalize: 3/(√5 - √2)', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["(√5 + √2)", "√5 - √2", "(3√5 + 3√2)/3", "√5 + √2"]', '√5 + √2', 'Multiply by (√5+√2)/(√5+√2): 3(√5+√2)/3 = √5 + √2', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_004', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Solve: 2^(2x) - 5(2^x) + 4 = 0', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["x = 0, 1", "x = 0, 2", "x = 1, 2", "x = -1, 2"]', 'x = 0, 2', 'Let y = 2^x. y² - 5y + 4 = 0 → y = 1 or 4. So x = 0 or 2', 'hard', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_005', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Express (2x+3)/((x-1)(x+2)) in partial fractions', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["5/(3(x-1)) + 1/(3(x+2))", "5/(3(x-1)) - 1/(3(x+2))", "1/(x-1) + 1/(x+2)", "5/(x-1) - 1/(x+2)"]', '5/(3(x-1)) + 1/(3(x+2))', 'A = 5/3, B = 1/3', 'hard', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_006', 'topic_wassce_em_algebra', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Simplify: log₈64 - log₂₇9', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["0", "1", "2/3", "4/3"]', '4/3', 'log₈64 = 2, log₂₇9 = 2/3. Result: 2 - 2/3 = 4/3', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_007', 'topic_wassce_em_polynomials', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'If (x-2) is a factor of f(x) = x³ - 3x² + kx + 2, find k', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["0", "1", "-1", "2"]', 'B', 'f(2) = 8 - 12 + 2k + 2 = 0 → 2k = 2 → k = 1.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_008', 'topic_wassce_em_polynomials', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For 2x² - 5x + 1 = 0 with roots α and β, find α² + β²', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["21/4", "17/4", "25/4", "9/4"]', '21/4', '(α+β)² - 2αβ = 25/4 - 1 = 21/4', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_009', 'topic_wassce_em_polynomials', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find remainder when x⁴ - 2x³ + 3x - 1 is divided by (x+1)', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["1", "-1", "3", "-5"]', '-1', 'f(-1) = 1 + 2 - 3 - 1 = -1', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_010', 'topic_wassce_em_polynomials', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One root of x² + px + q = 0 is twice the other. If p = -6, find q', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["4", "6", "8", "12"]', 'C', 'Roots r and 2r. Sum = 3r = 6 → r = 2. Product = 2r² = 8', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_011', 'topic_wassce_em_polynomials', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'For x² - 3x + 2 = 0 with roots α, β, find equation with roots 1/α and 1/β', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["2x² - 3x + 1 = 0", "x² - 3x + 2 = 0", "2x² + 3x + 1 = 0", "x² + 3x + 2 = 0"]', '2x² - 3x + 1 = 0', 'New sum = 3/2, product = 1/2 → 2x² - 3x + 1 = 0', 'hard', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_012', 'topic_wassce_em_sequences', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'AP: 5th term = 21, 10th term = 41. Find first term', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["3", "5", "7", "9"]', 'B', 'a + 4d = 21, a + 9d = 41 → d = 4, a = 5', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_013', 'topic_wassce_em_sequences', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find sum of first 20 terms: 3, 7, 11, 15, ...', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["820", "780", "840", "760"]', 'A', 'S₂₀ = 10[6 + 76] = 820', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_014', 'topic_wassce_em_sequences', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'GP: 3rd term = 12, 6th term = 96. Find common ratio', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["2", "3", "4", "1/2"]', 'A', 'r³ = 96/12 = 8 → r = 2', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_015', 'topic_wassce_em_sequences', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find S∞ for GP: 8, 4, 2, 1, ...', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["15", "16", "14", "12"]', 'B', 'S∞ = 8/(1-0.5) = 16', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_016', 'topic_wassce_em_sequences', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'How many terms of 5, 8, 11, ... give sum 155?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["8", "9", "10", "11"]', 'C', 'n(3n+7)/2 = 155 → n = 10', 'hard', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_017', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find dy/dx if y = (3x² + 2)⁵', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["5(3x² + 2)⁴", "30x(3x² + 2)⁴", "6x(3x² + 2)⁴", "15x(3x² + 2)⁴"]', '30x(3x² + 2)⁴', 'Chain rule: 5(3x²+2)⁴ × 6x', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_018', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Differentiate y = x²sin x', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["2x sin x + x² cos x", "2x cos x", "x² cos x - 2x sin x", "2x sin x - x² cos x"]', '2x sin x + x² cos x', 'Product rule', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_019', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find gradient of y = x³ - 3x² + 2 at x = 2', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["0", "2", "4", "-2"]', 'A', 'dy/dx = 3x² - 6x. At x=2: 12-12 = 0', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_020', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'y = x³ - 6x² + 9x + 1 has maximum at x =', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["1", "2", "3", "0"]', 'A', 'd²y/dx² < 0 at x = 1', 'hard', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_021', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'If y = e^(2x) + ln(3x), find dy/dx', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["2e^(2x) + 3/x", "2e^(2x) + 1/x", "e^(2x) + 1/x", "2e^(2x) + 1/(3x)"]', '2e^(2x) + 1/x', '2e^(2x) + 1/x', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_022', 'topic_wassce_em_differentiation', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 's = t³ - 6t² + 9t. When is velocity zero?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["t = 1 and t = 3", "t = 2 only", "t = 0 and t = 3", "t = 1 only"]', 't = 1 and t = 3', 'v = 3(t-1)(t-3) = 0', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_023', 'topic_wassce_em_integration', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Evaluate ∫(3x² + 2x - 1)dx', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["x³ + x² - x + C", "6x + 2 + C", "x³ + x² + x + C", "3x³ + x² - x + C"]', 'x³ + x² - x + C', 'Integrate term by term', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_024', 'topic_wassce_em_integration', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Find ∫(2x + 3)⁴ dx', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["(2x + 3)⁵/10 + C", "(2x + 3)⁵/5 + C", "2(2x + 3)⁵ + C", "(2x + 3)⁵ + C"]', '(2x + 3)⁵/10 + C', 'Substitution: u⁵/10 + C', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_025', 'topic_wassce_em_integration', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Evaluate ∫₀² x² dx', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["8/3", "4", "2/3", "8"]', '8/3', '[x³/3]₀² = 8/3', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_026', 'topic_wassce_em_integration', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Area under y = x² from x = 0 to x = 3', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["9", "27", "3", "9/2"]', 'A', '[x³/3]₀³ = 9', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_em_027', 'topic_wassce_em_integration', 'subj_wassce_elect_math', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Evaluate ∫₀^(π/2) cos x dx', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["0", "1", "-1", "2"]', 'B', '[sin x]₀^(π/2) = 1', 'easy', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
