('q_eng_2023_049', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2023_1', 'The words "export" (noun) and "export" (verb) differ in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Spelling", "B. Number of syllables", "C. Stress pattern", "D. Meaning only"]', 'C', 'EX-port (noun) vs ex-PORT (verb) differ in stress placement.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 49, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2023_050', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2023_1', 'Which word ends with the /z/ sound?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Books", "B. Cats", "C. Dogs", "D. Maps"]', 'C', 'The plural "s" in "dogs" is pronounced /z/ after voiced consonants.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 50, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the word that best completes the sentence: The manager''s decision was _____ by all the employees.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. applauded", "B. applaud", "C. applauding", "D. applauds"]', 'A', 'The passive voice requires the past participle "applauded".', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Select the correct option: Neither the teacher nor the students _____ present.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. was", "B. were", "C. is", "D. are"]', 'B', 'When "neither...nor" connects subjects, the verb agrees with the nearer subject (students - plural).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The word "ubiquitous" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. rare", "B. present everywhere", "C. dangerous", "D. beautiful"]', 'B', 'Ubiquitous means being present, appearing, or found everywhere.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct spelling:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. accomodation", "B. acommodation", "C. accommodation", "D. acomodation"]', 'C', 'Accommodation has two c''s and two m''s.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The opposite of "benevolent" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. kind", "B. generous", "C. malevolent", "D. caring"]', 'C', 'Benevolent means well-meaning and kindly; malevolent means having evil intentions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Identify the figure of speech: "The wind whispered through the trees."', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Simile", "B. Metaphor", "C. Personification", "D. Hyperbole"]', 'C', 'Personification gives human qualities (whispering) to non-human things (wind).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct form: If I _____ rich, I would travel the world.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. am", "B. was", "C. were", "D. be"]', 'C', 'In conditional sentences expressing hypothetical situations, "were" is used for all subjects.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The phrase "to burn the midnight oil" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. to waste resources", "B. to work late into the night", "C. to start a fire", "D. to cook at night"]', 'B', 'This idiom means to work or study late into the night.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Which sentence is grammatically correct?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. He don''t know the answer", "B. He doesn''t knows the answer", "C. He doesn''t know the answer", "D. He don''t knows the answer"]', 'C', 'Third person singular requires "doesn''t" + base form of verb.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'A word that sounds the same as another but has different meaning is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Synonym", "B. Antonym", "C. Homophone", "D. Homograph"]', 'C', 'Homophones are words that sound alike but differ in meaning (e.g., "there" and "their").', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct preposition: She arrived _____ the airport on time.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. in", "B. at", "C. on", "D. by"]', 'B', 'We use "at" with specific locations like airports, stations, etc.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The literary device used in "She sells seashells by the seashore" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Assonance", "B. Alliteration", "C. Onomatopoeia", "D. Consonance"]', 'B', 'Alliteration is the repetition of initial consonant sounds (s sounds).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Which word is an adverb?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Quick", "B. Quickly", "C. Quicker", "D. Quickest"]', 'B', 'Adverbs typically end in -ly and modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverbs.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The passive form of "The cat caught the mouse" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The mouse was caught by the cat", "B. The mouse is caught by the cat", "C. The mouse caught the cat", "D. The cat was caught by the mouse"]', 'A', 'In passive voice, the object becomes the subject and the verb becomes "was + past participle".', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct word: The news _____ shocking.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. are", "B. were", "C. is", "D. have been"]', 'C', '"News" is an uncountable noun and takes a singular verb.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The word "gregarious" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. shy and reserved", "B. fond of company", "C. angry and hostile", "D. lazy and slow"]', 'B', 'Gregarious means enjoying the company of others; sociable.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Identify the noun clause: "I know what you did last summer."', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. I know", "B. what you did", "C. what you did last summer", "D. last summer"]', 'C', 'The noun clause "what you did last summer" functions as the object of "know".', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
