('q_eng_2024_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the word closest in meaning to "candid":', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. secretive", "B. frank", "C. hostile", "D. timid"]', 'B', 'Candid means truthful and straightforward; frank.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The plural of "crisis" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. crisises", "B. crises", "C. crisis", "D. crisies"]', 'B', 'Greek-origin words ending in -is change to -es in plural form.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Which sentence contains an infinitive phrase?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Running is fun", "B. She wants to dance", "C. He danced beautifully", "D. Dancing makes her happy"]', 'B', '"To dance" is an infinitive phrase (to + base verb).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The expression "a blessing in disguise" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. something bad that seems good", "B. something good that seems bad at first", "C. a hidden treasure", "D. a religious gift"]', 'B', 'A blessing in disguise is something that initially appears negative but turns out to be beneficial.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct sentence:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Each of the boys have their books", "B. Each of the boys has his book", "C. Each of the boys have his book", "D. Each of the boys has their books"]', 'B', '"Each" is singular and requires "has" and "his" for agreement.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'A "paradox" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. a type of poem", "B. a contradictory statement that may be true", "C. a comparison using like", "D. an exaggeration"]', 'B', 'A paradox is a seemingly contradictory statement that reveals a truth upon reflection.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The word "ameliorate" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. to worsen", "B. to improve", "C. to destroy", "D. to ignore"]', 'B', 'Ameliorate means to make something bad better; improve.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct option: The committee _____ divided on the issue.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. is", "B. are", "C. was", "D. All of the above"]', 'D', 'Collective nouns can take singular or plural verbs depending on whether the group acts as one or as individuals.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Identify the type of sentence: "Although he was tired, he continued working."', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Simple", "B. Compound", "C. Complex", "D. Compound-complex"]', 'C', 'A complex sentence has one independent clause and at least one dependent clause.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The word "ephemeral" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. lasting forever", "B. short-lived", "C. very large", "D. extremely cold"]', 'B', 'Ephemeral means lasting for a very short time.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Which is a compound word?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Running", "B. Happiness", "C. Sunflower", "D. Beautiful"]', 'C', 'Sunflower is formed by combining two words: sun + flower.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correct relative pronoun: The book _____ I read was interesting.', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. who", "B. whom", "C. which", "D. whose"]', 'C', '"Which" is used for things; "who/whom" for people.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The phrase "to let the cat out of the bag" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. to release an animal", "B. to reveal a secret", "C. to open a bag", "D. to catch something"]', 'B', 'This idiom means to accidentally reveal a secret or surprise.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Identify the adjective clause: "The man who lives next door is a doctor."', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The man", "B. who lives next door", "C. is a doctor", "D. next door"]', 'B', 'The adjective clause "who lives next door" modifies the noun "man".', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The word "taciturn" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. talkative", "B. reserved in speech", "C. aggressive", "D. cheerful"]', 'B', 'Taciturn means reserved or uncommunicative in speech; saying little.', 'hard', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Choose the correctly punctuated sentence:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Where are you going.", "B. Where are you going?", "C. Where are you going!", "D. Where are you, going"]', 'B', 'Questions require a question mark at the end.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The figure of speech in "Life is a journey" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Simile", "B. Metaphor", "C. Personification", "D. Hyperbole"]', 'B', 'A metaphor directly compares two unlike things without using "like" or "as".', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'Which word is a conjunction?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Quickly", "B. However", "C. Beautiful", "D. Running"]', 'B', '"However" is a conjunctive adverb used to connect ideas.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_eng_2024_036', NULL, 'subj_wassce_english', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_eng_2024_1', 'The words "write" and "right" are examples of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Synonyms", "B. Antonyms", "C. Homophones", "D. Homographs"]', 'C', 'Homophones sound the same but have different meanings and spellings.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 36, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
