('q_fr_oral_005', 'topic_fr_oral', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Je ne comprends pas" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["I don''t know","I don''t understand","I don''t like","I don''t want"]', 'I don''t understand', 'Comprendre = to understand. Je ne comprends pas = I don''t understand.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_read_001', 'topic_fr_reading', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In French reading, "Il fait beau" describes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Bad weather","Good weather","Cold weather","Rainy weather"]', 'Good weather', 'Il fait beau means the weather is nice/beautiful.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_read_002', 'topic_fr_reading', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Marie a quinze ans" means Marie is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["15 years old","50 years old","5 years old","25 years old"]', '15 years old', 'Quinze = 15. "A...ans" means "is...years old".', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_read_003', 'topic_fr_reading', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Il habite à Paris" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["He works in Paris","He lives in Paris","He visits Paris","He leaves Paris"]', 'He lives in Paris', 'Habiter = to live. Il habite = he lives.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_read_004', 'topic_fr_reading', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'When you see "parce que" in a text, it indicates:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Time","Reason/Because","Place","Manner"]', 'Reason/Because', 'Parce que means "because" and introduces a reason.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_read_005', 'topic_fr_reading', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Chaque jour" in a passage means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Some days","Every day","One day","No day"]', 'Every day', 'Chaque = each/every. Chaque jour = every day.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_voc_002', 'topic_fr_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Comment dit-on "school" en français?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["maison","école","hôpital","église"]', 'école', 'École means school. Maison=house, hôpital=hospital, église=church.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_voc_003', 'topic_fr_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Aujourd''hui" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Yesterday","Tomorrow","Today","Always"]', 'Today', 'Aujourd''hui means today. Hier=yesterday, demain=tomorrow.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_voc_004', 'topic_fr_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The French word for "water" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["pain","lait","eau","jus"]', 'eau', 'Eau means water. Pain=bread, lait=milk, jus=juice.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_voc_005', 'topic_fr_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Frère" and "sœur" mean:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Father and mother","Brother and sister","Son and daughter","Uncle and aunt"]', 'Brother and sister', 'Frère = brother, sœur = sister.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_writ_001', 'topic_fr_writing', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A formal French letter begins with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Salut","Cher ami","Monsieur/Madame","Bonjour mon ami"]', 'Monsieur/Madame', 'Formal letters use Monsieur/Madame. Salut and Cher ami are informal.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_writ_002', 'topic_fr_writing', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To end a formal letter, you write:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Bisous","À bientôt","Veuillez agréer mes salutations distinguées","Salut"]', 'Veuillez agréer mes salutations distinguées', 'Formal closing uses "Veuillez agréer..." Others are informal.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_writ_003', 'topic_fr_writing', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In French, the date is written as:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Month, day, year","Day, month, year","Year, month, day","Day, year, month"]', 'B', 'French dates use day, month, year format: le 15 janvier 2024.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_writ_004', 'topic_fr_writing', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An informal letter to a friend starts with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Monsieur","Cher/Chère + name","Madame","À qui de droit"]', 'B', 'Informal letters use Cher (dear) + the person''s name.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_fr_writ_005', 'topic_fr_writing', 'subj_wassce_french', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To express an opinion in French, you can use:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Je pense que...","Il fait...","Il y a...","C''est..."]', 'Je pense que...', 'Je pense que (I think that) introduces an opinion.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_001', 'topic_geo_physical', 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The three main types of rocks are:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Granite, marble, slate","Igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic","Volcanic, plutonic, organic","Primary, secondary, tertiary"]', 'Igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic', 'Rocks are classified into three main types: igneous (from molten magma), sedimentary (from deposited materials), and metamorphic (transformed by heat/pressure).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_002', 'topic_geo_climate', 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The instrument used to measure atmospheric pressure is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Thermometer","Anemometer","Barometer","Hygrometer"]', 'C', 'A barometer measures atmospheric pressure. Thermometer measures temperature, anemometer measures wind speed, and hygrometer measures humidity.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_003', 'topic_geo_population', 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The movement of people from rural to urban areas is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Immigration","Emigration","Rural-urban migration","Urbanization"]', 'Rural-urban migration', 'Rural-urban migration is the movement of people from countryside to cities. Urbanization is the overall process of urban growth.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_004', 'topic_geo_mapwork', 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'On a map with scale 1:50,000, a distance of 4cm represents:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["2 km","4 km","20 km","50 km"]', '2 km', '1:50,000 means 1cm = 50,000cm = 500m = 0.5km. Therefore, 4cm = 4 x 0.5km = 2km.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_005', 'topic_geo_ghana', 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The largest lake in Ghana is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Lake Bosomtwe","Lake Volta","Lake Chad","Lake Victoria"]', 'Lake Volta', 'Lake Volta is the largest lake in Ghana and one of the largest man-made lakes in the world, created by the Akosombo Dam.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The breaking of rocks by plant roots is an example of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Chemical weathering", "B. Physical weathering", "C. Biological weathering", "D. Mechanical weathering"]', 'C', 'Biological weathering occurs when living organisms like plant roots break down rocks.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'A rift valley is formed by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Folding of rocks", "B. Faulting and subsidence", "C. Volcanic activity", "D. Erosion by rivers"]', 'B', 'Rift valleys form when land between two parallel faults subsides due to tensional forces.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Marble is formed from the metamorphism of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Granite", "B. Sandstone", "C. Limestone", "D. Shale"]', 'C', 'Marble forms when limestone undergoes metamorphism under heat and pressure.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'An ox-bow lake is formed from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Volcanic crater", "B. Cut-off river meander", "C. Glacial depression", "D. Coastal erosion"]', 'B', 'An ox-bow lake forms when a river meander is cut off from the main channel.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The wearing away of the sea bed is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Attrition", "B. Corrasion", "C. Hydraulic action", "D. Abrasion"]', 'D', 'Abrasion is the wearing away of the sea bed by waves carrying sand and pebbles.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Soil creep is a type of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Chemical weathering", "B. Mass movement", "C. Water erosion", "D. Wind erosion"]', 'B', 'Soil creep is the slow, downhill movement of soil particles due to gravity.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'A spit is formed by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. River deposition", "B. Coastal deposition", "C. Glacial erosion", "D. Wind erosion"]', 'B', 'A spit is a narrow ridge of sand or shingle extending from the coast, formed by longshore drift.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The continental crust is made mainly of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Basalt", "B. Granite", "C. Iron", "D. Nickel"]', 'B', 'Continental crust is mainly composed of granite (sial - silicon and aluminum).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'A volcanic mountain with a depression at the top is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Cone", "B. Crater", "C. Caldera", "D. Vent"]', 'B', 'A crater is the depression at the top of a volcano formed by eruption or collapse.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Loess is deposited by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Rivers", "B. Glaciers", "C. Wind", "D. Sea waves"]', 'C', 'Loess is fine, wind-blown sediment that forms fertile soil when deposited.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The hottest part of the day is usually around:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 12 noon", "B. 2 pm", "C. 4 pm", "D. 6 pm"]', 'B', 'Maximum temperature usually occurs around 2 pm due to heat lag - time for ground to heat up and warm the air.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The savanna vegetation is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Dense forest cover", "B. Tall grasses with scattered trees", "C. Evergreen trees", "D. No vegetation"]', 'B', 'Savanna has tall grasses with scattered drought-resistant trees like acacia and baobab.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Fog forms when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Air rises rapidly", "B. Air cools below its dew point near the ground", "C. Rain falls heavily", "D. Wind speed increases"]', 'B', 'Fog forms when air near the ground cools below its dew point, causing water vapor to condense.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The trade winds blow from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Equator to poles", "B. Subtropical highs to equatorial lows", "C. Poles to equator", "D. West to east"]', 'B', 'Trade winds blow from subtropical high pressure zones towards the equatorial low pressure zone.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Mangrove vegetation is found in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Desert regions", "B. Mountain tops", "C. Coastal swamps", "D. Temperate forests"]', 'C', 'Mangroves grow in coastal swamps and tidal areas with salt or brackish water.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Temperature decreases with altitude at a rate of about:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1°C per 100m", "B. 6.5°C per 1000m", "C. 10°C per 500m", "D. 2°C per 200m"]', 'B', 'The environmental lapse rate is approximately 6.5°C per 1000m of altitude gain.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Desert vegetation includes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mahogany trees", "B. Cacti and thorn bushes", "C. Tropical rainforest", "D. Coniferous trees"]', 'B', 'Desert plants like cacti and thorn bushes are adapted to conserve water in arid conditions.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The ITCZ is associated with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Dry conditions", "B. Heavy rainfall", "C. Cold temperatures", "D. High pressure"]', 'B', 'The Inter-Tropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ) is a low pressure zone where trade winds meet, causing heavy rainfall.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Deforestation leads to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Increased rainfall", "B. Soil erosion and climate change", "C. Improved soil fertility", "D. Reduced flooding"]', 'B', 'Deforestation causes soil erosion, loss of biodiversity, and contributes to climate change.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The tropical rainforest has:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. One layer of trees", "B. Two layers of trees", "C. Multiple canopy layers", "D. No tree cover"]', 'C', 'Tropical rainforests have multiple layers: emergent, canopy, understory, and forest floor.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'A topographical map shows:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Only roads and buildings", "B. Physical and human features", "C. Only population data", "D. Only political boundaries"]', 'B', 'Topographical maps show both physical features (relief, rivers) and human features (roads, settlements).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'The gradient of a slope is calculated by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Horizontal distance ÷ Vertical rise", "B. Vertical rise ÷ Horizontal distance", "C. Horizontal distance × Vertical rise", "D. Vertical rise + Horizontal distance"]', 'B', 'Gradient = Vertical rise ÷ Horizontal distance, often expressed as a ratio (e.g., 1:10).', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'Isobars on a map join places with equal:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Temperature", "B. Rainfall", "C. Atmospheric pressure", "D. Height"]', 'C', 'Isobars are lines connecting places with equal atmospheric pressure.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'If it is 12 noon at Greenwich, what time is it at 45°E?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 9 am", "B. 3 pm", "C. 6 pm", "D. 12 midnight"]', 'B', 'Each 15° of longitude equals 1 hour. 45°E ÷ 15 = 3 hours ahead. So 12 noon + 3 = 3 pm.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geo_2023_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_geo_2023_1', 'A choropleth map uses:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Dots to show distribution", "B. Shading to show data variations", "C. Lines to show movement", "D. Symbols to show locations"]', 'B', 'Choropleth maps use different shades or colors to show variations in data across areas.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
