('q_geog_phys_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A delta is formed at:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Mountain tops","River mouths","Ocean depths","Lake centers"]', 'River mouths', 'Deltas form where rivers deposit sediment at their mouths, often entering the sea.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geog_phys_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The water cycle includes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Evaporation, condensation, precipitation","Only rainfall","Only evaporation","Photosynthesis"]', 'Evaporation, condensation, precipitation', 'The hydrological cycle involves evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_geog_phys_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_geography', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An earthquake occurs due to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Wind movement","Movement of tectonic plates","Heavy rainfall","Human activities only"]', 'Movement of tectonic plates', 'Earthquakes result from sudden movement or fracture of tectonic plates.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_001', 'topic_gov_intro', 'subj_wassce_government', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The institution through which the state exercises its authority is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Nation","Country","Government","Society"]', 'Government', 'Government is the institution through which the state exercises its authority to make and enforce laws and policies.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_002', 'topic_gov_constitution', 'subj_wassce_government', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A rigid constitution is one that:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Can be easily amended","Requires special procedures to amend","Is unwritten","Has no amendment process"]', 'Requires special procedures to amend', 'A rigid constitution requires special procedures (like supermajority votes or referendums) to be amended, unlike a flexible constitution.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_003', 'topic_gov_organs', 'subj_wassce_government', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The arm of government responsible for making laws is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Executive","Legislature","Judiciary","Civil Service"]', 'Legislature', 'The Legislature (Parliament/Congress) is responsible for making laws. The Executive implements laws, and the Judiciary interprets them.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_004', 'topic_gov_systems', 'subj_wassce_government', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In a federal system of government:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Power is concentrated at the center","Power is shared between central and regional governments","There is only one level of government","The president has absolute power"]', 'Power is shared between central and regional governments', 'Federalism involves the constitutional division of powers between the central (federal) government and regional (state) governments.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_005', 'topic_gov_ghana', 'subj_wassce_government', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Ghana returned to constitutional rule in the Fourth Republic in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["1957","1981","1992","2000"]', 'C', 'Ghana''s Fourth Republic began on January 7, 1993, following the 1992 constitution and elections.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_001', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Power in a democracy is derived from:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. The military", "B. The people", "C. Traditional rulers", "D. Foreign powers"]', 'B', 'In a democracy, political power is derived from the people who are the ultimate source of authority.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_002', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Which of the following is NOT an organ of government?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Executive", "B. Legislature", "C. Judiciary", "D. Political party"]', 'D', 'Political parties are not organs of government. The three organs are executive, legislature, and judiciary.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 2, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_003', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The concept of legitimacy refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Legal authority", "B. Popular acceptance of authority", "C. Military power", "D. Economic strength"]', 'B', 'Legitimacy refers to the popular acceptance of a government as being rightfully in power.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 3, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_004', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Authority differs from power in that it is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Based on force", "B. Recognized as legitimate", "C. Always absolute", "D. Never challenged"]', 'B', 'Authority is power that is recognized as legitimate and rightful by those subject to it.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 4, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_005', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'A totalitarian state is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Limited government", "B. Complete state control", "C. Free press", "D. Multi-party system"]', 'B', 'A totalitarian state exercises complete control over all aspects of public and private life.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 5, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_006', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Which political ideology advocates for government ownership of production?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Capitalism", "B. Socialism", "C. Fascism", "D. Anarchism"]', 'B', 'Socialism advocates for collective or government ownership of the means of production.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 6, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_gov_2023_007', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Communism was developed by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Adam Smith", "B. Karl Marx", "C. John Locke", "D. Plato"]', 'B', 'Karl Marx developed the theory of communism along with Friedrich Engels.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 7, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_008', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'A constitution serves to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Limit government power", "B. Give absolute power", "C. Eliminate opposition", "D. Reduce democracy"]', 'A', 'A constitution serves to define and limit the powers of government while protecting citizens'' rights.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 8, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_009', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Rigid constitutions are difficult to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Understand", "B. Amend", "C. Implement", "D. Write"]', 'B', 'Rigid constitutions require special procedures and often supermajorities to amend.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 9, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_010', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'An unwritten constitution relies heavily on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Statutes and conventions", "B. Single document", "C. Military decrees", "D. Foreign laws"]', 'A', 'Unwritten constitutions are based on statutes, conventions, and judicial decisions rather than a single document.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 10, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_011', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The civil service is expected to be:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Partisan", "B. Neutral", "C. Elected", "D. Military-based"]', 'B', 'The civil service is expected to be politically neutral and serve any government in power.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 11, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_012', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Which of these is a function of the legislature?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Executing laws", "B. Making laws", "C. Judging cases", "D. Appointing ministers"]', 'B', 'The primary function of the legislature is law-making.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 12, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_013', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The Speaker of Parliament is responsible for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Executing laws", "B. Presiding over debates", "C. Leading the majority party", "D. Appointing judges"]', 'B', 'The Speaker presides over parliamentary debates and maintains order in the house.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 13, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_014', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Judicial review is the power to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Make laws", "B. Review laws for constitutionality", "C. Execute judgments", "D. Elect judges"]', 'B', 'Judicial review is the power of courts to examine laws and government actions for constitutionality.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 14, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_015', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'An independent judiciary is important for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Partisan politics", "B. Protecting rights", "C. Military control", "D. Executive dominance"]', 'B', 'An independent judiciary is crucial for protecting citizens'' rights and upholding the rule of law.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 15, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_016', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Local government exists to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Replace central government", "B. Bring government closer to the people", "C. Eliminate democracy", "D. Control the military"]', 'B', 'Local government brings governance closer to the people and addresses local needs.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 16, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_017', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The chief executive of a local council is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. President", "B. Chief Executive Officer", "C. Governor", "D. Paramount Chief"]', 'B', 'In Ghana, the head of a Metropolitan, Municipal, or District Assembly is called the Chief Executive.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 17, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_018', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Public corporations are established to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Make private profit", "B. Provide essential services", "C. Replace government", "D. Reduce employment"]', 'B', 'Public corporations are established to provide essential services to citizens.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 18, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_019', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The term "red tape" refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Government efficiency", "B. Bureaucratic delays", "C. Quick service", "D. Military rule"]', 'B', 'Red tape refers to excessive bureaucracy and administrative procedures that cause delays.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 19, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_020', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Decentralization involves:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Concentrating power at center", "B. Distributing power to lower levels", "C. Military takeover", "D. Eliminating local government"]', 'B', 'Decentralization is the transfer of authority and responsibility from central to local government.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 20, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_021', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'A one-party state is characterized by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Multiple parties", "B. Single legal party", "C. No government", "D. Foreign rule"]', 'B', 'A one-party state allows only one political party to hold power.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 21, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_022', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The main disadvantage of a two-party system is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Political stability", "B. Limited voter choice", "C. Strong government", "D. Clear mandate"]', 'B', 'A two-party system limits voter choice to essentially two political options.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 22, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_023', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'A coalition government is formed when:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. One party wins majority", "B. Parties combine to form government", "C. Military takes over", "D. Elections are cancelled"]', 'B', 'A coalition government is formed when no single party has a majority and parties combine.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 23, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_024', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The electoral commission is responsible for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Making laws", "B. Organizing elections", "C. Judging cases", "D. Forming government"]', 'B', 'The electoral commission is responsible for organizing and conducting elections.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 24, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_025', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Voter registration is important because it:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Prevents elections", "B. Ensures eligible persons vote", "C. Reduces turnout", "D. Eliminates parties"]', 'B', 'Voter registration ensures that only eligible citizens participate in elections.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 25, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_026', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Election rigging undermines:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Military rule", "B. Democratic principles", "C. One-party states", "D. Traditional authority"]', 'B', 'Election rigging undermines the democratic principles of free and fair elections.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 26, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_027', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'A plebiscite is similar to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. General election", "B. Referendum", "C. By-election", "D. Primary election"]', 'B', 'A plebiscite is similar to a referendum as both involve direct voting on specific issues.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 27, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_028', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The primary election is used to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Elect the president", "B. Select party candidates", "C. Form government", "D. Dissolve parliament"]', 'B', 'Primary elections are used to select candidates who will represent the party in general elections.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 28, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_029', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'An absolute majority means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 50% plus one vote", "B. Simple majority", "C. Two-thirds majority", "D. Unanimous vote"]', 'A', 'An absolute majority is more than half of all votes cast (50% plus one).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 29, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_030', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The opposition in parliament functions to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Support all government policies", "B. Criticize and provide alternatives", "C. Obstruct all legislation", "D. Form the government"]', 'B', 'The opposition''s role is to scrutinize government, criticize policies, and offer alternatives.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 30, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_031', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The first military coup in Ghana occurred in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1960", "B. 1966", "C. 1972", "D. 1979"]', 'B', 'The first military coup in Ghana occurred on February 24, 1966, overthrowing Nkrumah.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 31, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_032', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The Fourth Republic of Ghana began in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1979", "B. 1981", "C. 1992", "D. 2000"]', 'C', 'Ghana''s Fourth Republic began in 1992 under the new constitution.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 32, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_033', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'Nigeria gained independence in:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1957", "B. 1960", "C. 1963", "D. 1966"]', 'B', 'Nigeria gained independence from Britain on October 1, 1960.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 33, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_034', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The Biafran War in Nigeria occurred between:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 1960-1963", "B. 1967-1970", "C. 1975-1979", "D. 1983-1985"]', 'B', 'The Nigerian Civil War (Biafran War) lasted from 1967 to 1970.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, 34, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_gov_2023_035', NULL, 'subj_wassce_government', 'exam_wassce', 'paper_wassce_1', 'pp_wassce_gov_2023_1', 'The Convention People''s Party was founded by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. J.B. Danquah", "B. Kwame Nkrumah", "C. Kofi Busia", "D. William Ofori-Atta"]', 'B', 'Kwame Nkrumah founded the Convention People''s Party (CPP) in 1949.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, 35, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
