('q_twi_comp_005', 'topic_twi_comprehension', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'When a passage mentions "ɔman," it refers to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A house","A town/nation","A river","A market"]', 'B', 'Ɔman = town, nation, or state.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_compos_001', 'topic_twi_composition', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A formal Twi letter begins with:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Agya panyin","Me dɔfo","Owura/Awura","Adamfo"]', 'Owura/Awura', 'Owura (Mr.) / Awura (Mrs.) is used for formal letters.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_compos_002', 'topic_twi_composition', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To conclude a Twi essay, you can use:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Enti...","Ɛberɛ a...","Saa enti...","Nanso..."]', 'Saa enti...', 'Saa enti = therefore/in conclusion, summarizes the main point.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_compos_003', 'topic_twi_composition', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In descriptive writing, "ne ho yɛ" describes:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Location","Appearance/Beauty","Time","Sound"]', 'B', 'Ne ho yɛ fɛ = is beautiful. Used to describe appearance.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_compos_004', 'topic_twi_composition', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To express sequence in writing, use:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Kane...afei...akyiri no","Nanso","Enti","Anaa"]', 'Kane...afei...akyiri no', 'Kane = first, Afei = then, Akyiri no = finally - shows sequence.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_compos_005', 'topic_twi_composition', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A narrative essay in Twi is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Kasamu","Anansesɛm/Nsɛm a ɛkɔɔ so","Amammerɛ","Kasahyɛ"]', 'B', 'Anansesɛm or Nsɛm a ɛkɔɔ so = story/narrative.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_cul_002', 'topic_twi_culture', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Gye Nyame symbol represents:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Power of chiefs","Supremacy of God","Unity","Strength"]', 'Supremacy of God', 'Gye Nyame means "Except God" - representing God''s omnipotence.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_cul_003', 'topic_twi_culture', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Kente cloth is traditionally worn during:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Funerals only","Important ceremonies and festivals","Everyday activities","Farming"]', 'Important ceremonies and festivals', 'Kente is worn during special occasions like festivals, weddings, and ceremonies.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_cul_004', 'topic_twi_culture', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Akan naming ceremony is held:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["At birth","On the 8th day after birth","After one year","At puberty"]', 'On the 8th day after birth', 'The outdooring/naming ceremony (din to) is traditionally on the 8th day.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_cul_005', 'topic_twi_culture', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'In Akan society, inheritance is typically:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Patrilineal","Matrilineal","Bilateral","Through eldest child"]', 'Matrilineal', 'Akan inheritance is matrilineal - through the mother''s line.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_gram_002', 'topic_twi_grammar', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Mekɔ sukuu" means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["I go to school","I am at school","I left school","I like school"]', 'I go to school', 'Me = I, kɔ = go, sukuu = school. Mekɔ sukuu = I go to school.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_gram_003', 'topic_twi_grammar', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The plural marker in Twi is often:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["a-","n-/m-","e-","o-"]', 'n-/m-', 'Many Twi plurals are formed with the n- or m- prefix.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_gram_004', 'topic_twi_grammar', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Yɛn" in Twi means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["You (singular)","They","We/Us","He/She"]', 'We/Us', 'Yɛn = we/us (first person plural pronoun).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_gram_005', 'topic_twi_grammar', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To form a question in Twi, you typically:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Add ''anaa'' at the end","Change word order completely","Always use ''sɛn''","Add ''na'' at the beginning"]', 'Add ''anaa'' at the end', 'Questions in Twi often end with "anaa" for yes/no questions.', 'medium', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_voc_002', 'topic_twi_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Ɛda" in Twi means:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Day","Night","Week","Month"]', 'A', 'Ɛda = day. Anadwo = night.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_voc_003', 'topic_twi_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Twi word for "food" is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Nsuo","Aduane","Ntoma","Fie"]', 'B', 'Aduane = food. Nsuo = water, Ntoma = cloth, Fie = house.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_voc_004', 'topic_twi_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, '"Medaase" is used to say:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["Hello","Goodbye","Thank you","Please"]', 'Thank you', 'Medaase = Thank you (I lie down for you).', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_twi_voc_005', 'topic_twi_vocabulary', 'subj_wassce_twi', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The numbers "baako, mmienu, mmiɛnsa" mean:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["1, 2, 3","4, 5, 6","10, 20, 30","7, 8, 9"]', '1, 2, 3', 'Baako = 1, Mmienu = 2, Mmiɛnsa = 3.', 'easy', 3, 1, 30, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_01', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The organelle responsible for protein synthesis in cells is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mitochondria", "B. Ribosome", "C. Golgi apparatus", "D. Lysosome"]', 'B', 'Ribosomes are the sites of protein synthesis in cells.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_02', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Which of the following is NOT a function of the cell membrane?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Selective permeability", "B. Protection", "C. Protein synthesis", "D. Cell recognition"]', 'C', 'Protein synthesis occurs at ribosomes, not the cell membrane.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_03', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The powerhouse of the cell is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Nucleus", "B. Chloroplast", "C. Mitochondria", "D. Endoplasmic reticulum"]', 'C', 'Mitochondria produce ATP through cellular respiration.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_04', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Osmosis is the movement of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Solute from low to high concentration", "B. Water from high to low water potential", "C. Solute through a membrane", "D. Gases across a membrane"]', 'B', 'Osmosis is water movement from high to low water potential through a semi-permeable membrane.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_05', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Which organelle contains digestive enzymes?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Ribosome", "B. Lysosome", "C. Centrosome", "D. Nucleolus"]', 'B', 'Lysosomes contain hydrolytic enzymes for intracellular digestion.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z')
INSERT INTO "questions" (id, topic_id, subject_id, exam_type_id, paper_type_id, past_paper_id, question_text, question_type, round_type, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, points, marks, time_limit, question_number, section, is_compulsory, image_url, syllabus_topic_id, command_word, assessment_objective, source_paper_code, source_question_number, exam_board_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES
('q_wassce_bio_2023_06', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The control center of the cell is the:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Cytoplasm", "B. Cell membrane", "C. Nucleus", "D. Mitochondria"]', 'C', 'The nucleus contains DNA and controls cell activities.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_07', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Active transport differs from passive transport because it:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Does not require a membrane", "B. Requires energy (ATP)", "C. Only moves water", "D. Moves substances down a gradient"]', 'B', 'Active transport requires ATP to move substances against concentration gradient.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_08', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Plant cells differ from animal cells by having:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mitochondria", "B. Cell wall and chloroplasts", "C. Nucleus", "D. Ribosomes"]', 'B', 'Plant cells have cell walls and chloroplasts that animal cells lack.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_09', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The fluid mosaic model describes the structure of:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Cell wall", "B. Cytoplasm", "C. Cell membrane", "D. Nuclear envelope"]', 'C', 'The fluid mosaic model describes the cell membrane structure.', 'medium', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_10', NULL, 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Which type of cell division produces gametes?', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mitosis", "B. Meiosis", "C. Binary fission", "D. Budding"]', 'B', 'Meiosis produces haploid gametes for sexual reproduction.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_11', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'DNA stands for:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Deoxyribose nucleic acid", "B. Deoxyribonucleic acid", "C. Diribonucleic acid", "D. Deoxyribose nitrogen acid"]', 'B', 'DNA is deoxyribonucleic acid.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_12', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The genotype Aa represents:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Homozygous dominant", "B. Homozygous recessive", "C. Heterozygous", "D. Co-dominant"]', 'C', 'Aa has two different alleles, making it heterozygous.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_13', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'In humans, sex is determined by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. X chromosome from mother", "B. Y chromosome from father", "C. Number of autosomes", "D. Environmental factors"]', 'B', 'Males contribute either X or Y; Y determines male sex.', 'medium', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_14', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'A mutation is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Normal cell division", "B. A change in DNA sequence", "C. Protein synthesis", "D. Cell differentiation"]', 'B', 'Mutations are permanent changes in the DNA sequence.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_15', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The ratio 3:1 in Mendel''s experiments represents:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Genotypic ratio", "B. Phenotypic ratio in F2", "C. Sex ratio", "D. Mutation rate"]', 'B', 'The 3:1 ratio is the phenotypic ratio in F2 monohybrid crosses.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_16', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Sickle cell disease is caused by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Bacterial infection", "B. Viral infection", "C. Gene mutation", "D. Nutritional deficiency"]', 'C', 'Sickle cell is caused by a point mutation in the hemoglobin gene.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_17', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The base that pairs with adenine in DNA is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Guanine", "B. Cytosine", "C. Thymine", "D. Uracil"]', 'C', 'Adenine pairs with thymine (A-T) in DNA.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_18', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Crossing over occurs during:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Mitosis", "B. Meiosis I", "C. Meiosis II", "D. Interphase"]', 'B', 'Crossing over occurs during prophase I of meiosis.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_19', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'A pedigree chart is used to:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Classify organisms", "B. Trace inheritance patterns", "C. Count chromosomes", "D. Measure DNA"]', 'B', 'Pedigree charts trace inheritance patterns in families.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_20', 'topic_genetics', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The number of chromosomes in human body cells is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 23", "B. 44", "C. 46", "D. 48"]', 'C', 'Human body cells contain 46 chromosomes (23 pairs).', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_21', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'A community of living organisms and their physical environment is called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Population", "B. Ecosystem", "C. Biome", "D. Habitat"]', 'B', 'An ecosystem includes both biotic and abiotic components.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_22', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Organisms that make their own food are called:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Consumers", "B. Decomposers", "C. Producers", "D. Herbivores"]', 'C', 'Producers (autotrophs) make their own food through photosynthesis.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_23', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The nitrogen cycle involves all EXCEPT:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Nitrogen fixation", "B. Nitrification", "C. Photosynthesis", "D. Denitrification"]', 'C', 'Photosynthesis is part of the carbon cycle, not nitrogen cycle.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_24', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'A relationship where one organism benefits and the other is unaffected is:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Parasitism", "B. Mutualism", "C. Commensalism", "D. Competition"]', 'C', 'In commensalism, one benefits while the other is neither helped nor harmed.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_25', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Primary succession occurs on:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Burned forests", "B. Bare rock", "C. Abandoned farmland", "D. Flooded areas"]', 'B', 'Primary succession starts on bare, lifeless substrates like rock.', 'medium', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_26', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'The greenhouse effect is caused mainly by:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Oxygen", "B. Nitrogen", "C. Carbon dioxide", "D. Hydrogen"]', 'C', 'CO2 is a major greenhouse gas trapping heat in the atmosphere.', 'easy', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_27', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'In a food chain, energy transfer between trophic levels is approximately:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. 100%", "B. 50%", "C. 10%", "D. 1%"]', 'C', 'Only about 10% of energy transfers between trophic levels.', 'medium', 1, 1, 90, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
('q_wassce_bio_2023_28', 'topic_ecology', 'subj_wassce_biology', NULL, NULL, 'pp_wassce_bio_2023_1', 'Biological oxygen demand (BOD) indicates:', 'multiple_choice', NULL, '["A. Air quality", "B. Water pollution level", "C. Soil fertility", "D. Temperature"]', 'B', 'High BOD indicates organic pollution in water.', 'medium', 1, 1, 60, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z', '2026-08-04T00:00:00.000Z'),
